plus §4.3 (1458) and §4.4 for the Windows\n22|and broker rules. All clause citations name the pinned file, never\n23|the network, never v0.5.0.\n24|\n25|## Finding-by-finding table (verdict -> change -> test that fails without it -> evidence)\n26|\n27|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n28||---|---|---|---|\n29|| P2-A custody oracle looks through the wrapper; no narrowing admits a member the absence classifier must reject | `requireLocalError` now asserts the TOP-LEVEL `*Error` dynamic type plus no reachable `*axerror.Error` (the wrapper IS the observable refusal: the cause is redacted off the wire). Shipped `N-absence-remap-widen` in the reviewer's R05 shape (`runtimeAbsent` admitting `runtime mode`); kept `N-background-absence-remap` (rewritten to the platform conjunct after the `Request.Name` deletion) for the reject direction. Re-ran every custody row after the oracle change: none only passed because of the old helper | `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal` (a widened 0755 leaf maps to `capability_unavailable` under the mutant; the top-level assertion reddens). Proven load-bearing: the row SURVIVES under the old helper (reproduces R05) and KILLS under the fixed one | `harness-pass1/N-absence-remap-widen.log`, `harness-pass1/N-background-absence-remap.log` (+ pass 2), `plant-replays/N-absence-remap-widen.log` + `oracle-replay-old-verdict.log` (old-oracle SURVIVED replay) |\n30|| P2-B `Request.Name` re-opens the §3.2 divergence per call; the spec path pinned at the constants, not the entry | `Request.Name` DELETED: `Acquire` always passes `RuntimeDirName`, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths. `EnsureRuntimeDir`/`VerifyRuntimeDir` keep their `name` parameter for the grammar rows. New `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` through `Acquire` for foreground and background; rows 16/56 name it. The P01 probe is unstageable (the field does not exist) and R11 inapplicable | `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` (foreground, background subtests; any caller-selectable leaf or renamed constant reddens) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `internal/tmuxserver/acquire.go` |\n31|| P3-A absence remap pinned on the macOS axis only | `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` now drives macos, linux, and wsl2 subtests (the cold state is identical: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is tmpfs); named under row 52 | The linux/wsl2 subtests (the reviewer's R14 shape fails on both firsthand, macos still maps) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `R14-replay.log` (R14 plant: macos PASS, linux/wsl2 FAIL) |\n32|| P3-B censusable \"every background test arms a spy\" is false (7 of 11) | Armed the spy in all four (`TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid`, `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf`, the background half of `TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies`, the background iteration of `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform`, each asserting zero calls) and scoped the README/`acquire.go` sentence to background-path `Acquire` tests. Mechanical census: 12/12 armed (incl. the new background subtest) | The four tests' new zero-call assertions (a guarded `D-background-fallback`-shaped plant is visible to all of them) | `pkg-tests-v.log` |\n33|| Obs R03/ELOOP, unopenable root, Fchmod/Fsync/Stat arms, nested invocation, vacuous members | One-sentence TRACEABILITY entries: ELOOP darwin-equivalence under row 6 (reasoned, not run); the 0000-root arm and the `Fchmod`/`Fsync`/leaf-`Stat` arms under B15 as error-arm rows; the nested-invocation over-strict refusal under B16 (owner TASK-260830-1c28dz); the live-member scoping (`TMUXEnv`/`InheritedSocket` only) under row 23; the `localstore`-root caller contract stated as undriven under B19 | — (bounds/prose, no behavior) | `TRACEABILITY.md` rows 6/23, B15/B16/B19 |\n34|\n35|Kept untouched per the verdict: the dedicated-server rule per vector,\n36|the background broker-or-refuse wiring with the literal\n37|`capability_unavailable