er a typed same-user generation-bound broker principal. A stale\n72|  admission — the replayed-cached shape — refuses on both paths.\n73|- (5) Spawn argv: `BuildArgv` emits exactly\n74|  `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session`\n75|  through the landed argv gate. Native Windows refuses every request.\n76|\n77|Extended vs deliberately not extended (unchanged from rev4; the\n78|reviewer verified each claim rather than accepting it):\n79|\n80|- Extended (composed): `terminalbackend.Admitted` (attestation\n81|  verdict), `axpane` caller vocabulary, `axerror` typed refusal,\n82|  `scalar` platform/path/UUIDv7 grammars, `secprim` Guard /\n83|  `OpenNoFollowDir` / `CheckArgv`, the `localstore` Runtime IPC root\n84|  (`PathRuntime`, consumed as the caller-supplied `Request.Root` —\n85|  this leaf resolves no root of its own), the `hosttrust`\n86|  verify-never-repair precedent, the `termbind` crash-hook pattern.\n87|- Deliberately not extended: `hosttrust` custody itself (Host Channel\n88|  authority — a tmux runtime dir is not a trust store);\n89|  `terminalbackend` Reconcile evidence admission (consumed, not\n90|  re-owned); `axpane` checkRealm (unexported; this leaf composes the\n91|  same Has-plus-generation-equality over the probe-reported verdict);\n92|  the host-binding/provider-build cross-bind (stays with the lifecycle\n93|  owner, bound B13); `terminstance` lifecycle execution (sibling leaf);\n94|  `secprim`'s private `guardRootMatches` (mirrored as\n95|  `handleBoundToPath` with a seam because the original is unexported);\n96|  `internal/traceability` (untouched — bindings and the re-pin belong\n97|  to the final leaf).\n98|\n99|Determinism: every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs\n100|through injected dependencies. No test starts a tmux process; the\n101|suite passes with the tmux binary unresolvable and no tmux process on\n102|the host (71 top-level PASS, 0 SKIP in the tmux-hidden run). No AC row\n103|has a real-tmux witness — that is the design, not a gap (bound B1).\n104|\n105|## Coverage ratio (measured, not planned)\n106|\n107|**58 of 58 AC rows driven** through production entries by named\n108|committed tests — matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`,\n109|reproduced with spec-clause mapping in\n110|`TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md` (rev5). Rows 16/56 name the\n111|new entry-level spec-path test on both callers, row 52 names the\n112|macos/linux/wsl2 absence subtests and the top-level custody oracle,\n113|row 6 states the ELOOP equivalence, row 23 scopes the live collision\n114|members, and the mutant-to-gate map names all 55 narrowing rows.\n115|\n116|## Mutants (shipped harness, per-plant raw logs)\n117|\n118|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py` —\n119|55 narrowing + 1 supplementary additive (D-background-fallback,\n120|labeled) + 1 harmless SURVIVED control. Pass 1 and pass 2: **57/57\n121|each, verdict lists identical**, exit 0. Per-row raw logs (go output +\n122|subprocess exit) for both passes are in the evidence tarball;\n123|production blobs byte-identical before/after every run\n124|(`git status` shows only candidate paths). No token-preserving\n125|source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text (stated\n126|bound B4, harness executes the behavioral suite). The one\n127|nil-dependency narrowing that kills by panic (N-deps-foreground) is\n128|disclosed in the harness and the matrix; N-deps-background kills by\n129|an unavailable-vs-dependencies mismatch since the admitted request\n130|reaches Verify on the absent leaf. N-fchmod-umask and the\n131|read-only-root test assume a non-root test user (bound B14), the same\n132|shape as the reviewer's plant. N-broker-empty-generation,\n133|N-commit-eacces-as-exist, and the background leg of\n134|N-verify-absence-detail kill by reroute to a neighboring refusal,\n135|disclosed in their row notes. The reviewers' error-arm plants\n136|(stat-failure arms flipped to fail-open, the unreachable guard arm,\n137|the unopenable-root arm) are reported as error-arm rows under bound\n138|B15 and are never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n139|\n140|## Crash / idempotency (unchanged from rev4)\n141|\n142|Real SIGKILL seam (unix): `TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates`\n143|(child runs the genuine `EnsureRuntimeDir` entry and kills itself in\n144|`AfterMkdir`, after mkdirat and before verification plus parent\n145|fsync; parent proves the retry converges to the one verified\n146|directory). Idempotent replay: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent`,\n147|`TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently`,\n148|`TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry` (spawn-then-retry\n149|attaches with exactly one spawn). Crash convergence states the umask\n150|bound B10; the server socket's crash evidence is owned by the\n151|lifecycle leaf (bound B9).\n152|\n153|## Validation (all run firsthand in this session)\n154|\n155|Configured suite read from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`\n156|(count 30, verified by read). All 30 green, run by this run (nothing\n157|accepted from rev4 or from construction):\n158|\n159|- 1 gofmt clean (empty file list); 2 `go build ./...` exit 0;\n160|  3 `go vet ./...` exit 0.\n161|- 4 `go test ./... -count=1 -v` exit 0: 45/45 packages ok, 0 package\n162|  FAIL, 0 unindented test FAIL (the measured 21 indented `--- FAIL`\n163|  lines are kill excerpts logged by passing suites), 14\n164|  pre-existing SKIP outside this package, 0 SKIP in\n165|  `internal/tmuxserver`.\n166|- 5 race gate exit 0 with no DATA RACE: run in 6 bounded groups\n167|  (8/8/8/8/8/5 packages = all 45 from `go list ./...`) because one\n168|  shell call is time-bounded; same flags otherwise (`-race -count=1`).\n169|  45/45 ok.\n170|- 6 `go test ./... -cover -count=1` exit 0: 45/45 ok.\n171|  `go test ./internal/tmuxserver/ -cover` 92.6% statements.\n172|- 7-23 all 17 fuzz seeds exit 0. 24 tracecheck exit 0 (70/574).\n173|  25 cataloggen -check exit 0. 26 linux build exit 0. 27 windows build\n174|  exit 0. 28 JSON parse exit 0. 29 `task-board validate` exit 0 (with\n175|  the board's pre-existing 180 issues). 30 `git diff --check` exit 0.\n176|- Repository gates beyond the 30: `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet\n177|  ./...` exit 0, `GOOS=windows go test -c ./internal/tmuxserver`\n178|  exit 0, `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/tmuxserver` exit 0; package\n179|  suite 140 RUN / 71 top-level PASS / 69 subtest PASS / 0 SKIP;\n180|  tmux-hidden suite (`PATH` without tmux, `TMUX`/`TMUX_TMPDIR` unset,\n181|  no tmux process) exit 0 with 71 top-level PASS and 0 SKIP.\n182|\n183|Reran myself: everything above, plus the mutant battery (targeted\n184|subsets during development + two full logged passes). Accepted from\n185|already-attached evidence: nothing — rev4 evidence is superseded by\n186|this revision.\n187|\n188|`internal/traceability` untouched; README section updated (55-row\n189|battery count, scoped spy sentence) with exact test commands and no\n190|CLI/capability claim; LOGBOOK rev5 entry added newest-first. The\n191|candidate is UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n192|\n193|## Rejection-pattern self-check\n194|\n195|(a) Literals asserted from spec text at entries (`capability_unavailable`\n196|plus all five typed details, exit 6; `\"tmux\"`/`\"ax.sock\"` plus the\n197|joined `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` at `SocketPath` AND through `Acquire` on\n198|both callers; `ax`/`pane`/UUID session tail; `0700`\n199|on both the widened and narrower sides; caller vocabulary;\n200|`credential_capable_execution_realm` as the admitted member, including\n201|the both-empty pair), never production constants. (b) Every rule driven\n202|through the entry the matrix names; the creation gate is enforced by a\n203|call on the background miss path, custody refusals are staged through\n204|`Acquire` on both paths (including the verify-side non-directory leaf\n205|and the absence/missing-root split on the background entry, now on\n206|three platforms)