n authority: sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n20|verification, liveness, and expiry are the landed\n21|`internal/terminalbackend` Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission verdict,\n22|consumed here as an `Admitted` set composed only with the generation\n23|equality `internal/axpane` checkRealm enforces. This leaf decides\n24|membership plus generation binding and re-decides nothing.\n25|\n26|## §3.2 socket path and runtime root\n27|\n28|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n29||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n30|| 56 | Dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root (macOS: per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), resolved by the landed localstore layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity. The runtime leaf is not an Acquire input: the entry always passes RuntimeDirName, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths | `SocketPath` (socket.go), `Acquire` (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n31|\n32|## §4.2 dedicated -S server; no ambient/default discovery or reuse\n33|\n34|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n35||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n36|| 16 | AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server, as `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` with both leaves asserted as spec literals; the Acquire outcome socket equals `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths | `SocketPath` (socket.go), `Acquire` (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n37|| 17 | MUST NOT discover or reuse the default server by ambient socket name, under hostile ambient on all five members | `ResolveSocket` (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n38|| 18 | Ambient facts observed without use | `ObserveAmbient` (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, Test