e foreground entry pins via `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested` | **SURVIVED ×2** | K05 kills |\n82|| R18 | inside the miss arm, after `checkCreationAllowed` refuses: `if req.Deps.ProbeServer != nil && req.Deps.Spawn != nil { return acquireForeground(req, socket) }` | a background miss whose `Dependencies` carry the foreground probe — realistic, because the lifecycle adapter passes one shared `Dependencies` value to every caller | **SURVIVED ×2**: no committed background test arms `ProbeServer`, so the spy census (`Spawn`) never observes the fallback; the unguarded shape (`D-background-fallback`) is still killed by 11 tests | K04 kills |\n83|\n84|Why this is one class: the broker path drives exactly two server-admission shapes (`{gen, no\n85|rows}` as \"unattested server\" and `{rows, stale gen}` as \"stale server admission\") and one\n86|dependency shape (`Spawn` armed, `ProbeServer` nil). Rejection pattern (b) as stated in every\n87|brief of this task — \"if a rule is implemented TWICE (… an exported entry and its internal\n88|sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant\" — applies: the \"attested server\" rule is\n89|pinned at the helper (`TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct`) and at the foreground\n90|entry, but the broker-side wiring in `CheckBrokerContact` has no row that admits a member, and\n91|rows 27/28/31 are measured for one fixture each. The DoD lines \"negative tests that fail when the\n92|gate admits what it must reject\" and \"every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant\" are not met\n93|for the broker-side attested-server wiring; the no-fallback proof has a blind spot keyed on the\n94|sibling dependency. Production is correct today; the fix is tests plus rows:\n95|\n96|1. extend `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` with three subtests — zero\n97|   `RealmAdmission{}`, `{Admitted: realm row, RawGeneration: \"\"}`, `{Admitted: decoy only,\n98|   RawGeneration: bound}` — asserting the literal `capabilit