acquire.go:140-143 (\"Refusals precede side\n124|  effects: malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing dependencies all refuse before any directory\n125|  is created\") and results.md:61-62 (\"refuses malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing\n126|  dependencies before any side effect\"). Probe P01: a foreground request with `SessionID =\n127|  \"12345\"` **creates `<root>/tmux` and calls `ProbeServer` before** refusing `tmux_invalid_arguments\n128|  at session identity` (spawn 0). The session identity is malformed input; `acquireForeground`\n129|  validates it only inside `BuildArgv`, after `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe. Either parse the\n130|  session (`scalar.ParseUUIDv7`) at the `Acquire` entry before any side effect and add the\n131|  no-directory/no-probe assertions to `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` (row 45), or\n132|  reword both sentences to the members that are true (caller, realm details, root/name grammar,\n133|  override, collision, dependencies). Rejection pattern (f).\n134|\n135|## Observations (not findings; a sentence each in TRACEABILITY if the producer agrees)\n136|\n137|1. Probe P02: a comma inside the runtime root (`<root>/a,b`, admitted by the POSIX grammar) makes\n138|   `tmuxEnvSocket` split at the wrong comma, so a `TMUX` value naming the derived socket in the\n139|   real encoding walks past the collision gate and `Acquire` spawns. tmux(1) itself splits `TMUX`\n140|   at the first comma, so the decoding is faithful to the source of the encoding; worth a clause in\n141|   row 23/B16 (\"roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX member's encoding\").\n142|2. Probe P03: a cwd-relative spelling of the derived socket (`tmux/ax.sock` with the process cwd\n143|   at the root) walks past the cleaned-string collision gate — the same bound class as the B16\n144|   symlink alias (no path equivalence is applied); B16 could say \"symlinked or relative alias\".\n145|3. Probe P04: `Dependencies.Spawn` is inert on the background pat