x unresolvable | `go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1 -v -coverprofile`: 140 RUN, **71 top-level PASS, 69 subtest PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP**, 92.6% statements. Determinism holds; no real-tmux witness exists (bound B1, honest). The 12 uncovered blocks are the B15 error-arm class (two of them unnamed in B15's list), the `AfterMkdir` hook (exercised in the crash child, outside the coverprofile), the under-mutant-only `background fallback` arm (acquire.go:203), and one input-reachable arm not listed in B15 (observation 5) | `logs/pkg-tests-notmux-v.log`, `logs/tmuxserver-cover.out` |\n47|| Producer harness, two passes on the mutant copy | **57/57 both passes** (55 narrowing + D-background-fallback KILLED exit 1, C-control SURVIVED exit 0); verdict lists identical to each other and to the producer's attached pass 1 and pass 2; every raw log carries its `exit:` line; package files byte-identical to the candidate after each pass; zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` anywhere. Kill lines spot-checked against the row notes (`N-absence-remap-widen`: `err top-level type = *axerror.Error … want *tmuxserver.Error`; `N-background-absence-remap`: macos subtest; `D-background-fallback`: `spawn calls = 1, want 0` ×5; `N-containment-odirectory-verify`: `BLOCKED for 5s on a FIFO leaf`; `N-deps-foreground`: panic) | `harness-pass1/`, `harness-pass2/`, `logs/harness-pass*-verdicts.log` |\n48|| Producer evidence archive | real gzip; MANIFEST 143 entries, no self-entry, **143/143 sha256 verify**, no unlisted file; one raw log per plant per pass with `exit:` (57+57); producer pass1 == pass2 == reviewer rerun; race groups 8/8/8/8/8/5 = 45 packages, 0 `DATA RACE`; `pkg-tests-notmux-v.log` 140 RUN / 0 SKIP; `R14-replay.log` and `oracle-replay-old-verdict.log` show what they claim. `static-gates.log`, `cmd26/27/30` are 0-byte files: consistent with green commands that print nothing, but the archive records no exit code for the static gates — the exit claims for those live only in the results prose (observation 6; rerun and green here) | (checked in place) |\n49|| Old-oracle replay | With `requireLocalError` reverted to the rev4 `errors.As` body and the rev4 R05 mutant applied, the full package suite **passes (exit 0)**; with the committed top-level oracle the same mutant is KILLED (R03 below). The oracle fix is load-bearing, as the producer's replay claims | `logs/oracle-replay-old-R03.log` |\n50|| Reviewer battery, 20 rows × 2 passes | identical verdicts both passes; see §M | `battery/pass1/`, `battery/pass2/`, `battery/reviewer_battery.py` |\n51|| Reviewer probes, 11 tests | all behave as described in §P; K01-K05 pass on the untouched candidate and kill their rows | `logs/probes-rev5.log`, `battery/zz_review_probe_test.go` |\n52|| Boundary / hygiene | `internal/traceability` untouched (`git diff base tree -- internal/traceability` empty); no `0.5.0` citation; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR tree or any copy; no `os/exec`/`Getenv`/`Environ`/`localstore` import in any production file (comment mentions only); README section carries no `ax` command, `doctor` or capability claim; every one of the 69 test names in TRACEABILITY.md and in the conformance matrix exists in the committed suite; row count 58 verified (1..58, no gaps, no duplicates); every mutant named in TRACEABILITY/matrix exists in the harness (57 rows: 55 `N-`, `D-background-fallback`, `C-control`); LOGBOOK newest-first with the rev1 block superseded; `hosttrust.platformModeOK` (B17) and `localstore.InitializeLayout/ensureOwnerDirectory` 0700 (B19) precedents re-read and hold | `logs/static-gates.log` |\n53|\n54|## Closure of the rev4 findings (verified by driving, not by reading the results table)\n55|\n56|| rev4 | Closed? | How verified |\n57|| --- | --- | --- |\n58|| P2-A custody oracle looks through the wrapper; no admit-direction narrowing on `runtimeAbsent` | **yes** | `requireLocalError` asserts `err.(*Error)` AND `!errors.As(err, &*axerror.Error)`; rev4 R05 replayed as R03 → KILLED ×2 by `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal` (`err top-level type = *axerror.Error … want *tmuxserver.Error`); the containment member (R02) KILLED ×2 by `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf`; the old-oracle replay proves the helper is load-bearing; `N-absence-remap-widen` shipped and KILLED ×2 in the producer harness; `N-background-absence-remap` kept. The ownership member of the same class is the residue (P3-A below) |\n59|| P2-B `Request.Name` re-opens the §3.2 path per call | **yes** | The field is gone (`grep -n Name acquire.go` finds only `RuntimeDirName`); `Acquire` passes `RuntimeDirName` at all three sites; `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both callers; reviewer rows R04/R05/R06 (a `\"ax-tmux\"` literal at the lexical, ensure and verify sites respectively) KILLED ×2 by 18/8/6 tests including that test on the relevant caller |\n60|| P3-A absence remap pinned on macOS only | **yes** | `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` runs macos/linux/wsl2; rev4 R14 replayed as R07 → KILLED ×2 by the linux and wsl2 subtests exactly |\n61|| P3-B \"every background test arms a spy\" false for 4 of 11 | **yes** | Mechanical census: 12 background-path `Acquire` tests, 12 arm `spawnSpy` and assert zero calls (the 13th `CallerBackground` match is the helper test `TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground`, not an `Acquire` test); effect census R08 (a guarded direct-spawn plant at the top of `acquireBackground`) reddens 11 top-level tests / 20 lines — the 12th, `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform`, refuses at the lexical gate before the function is entered, which is correct. README and acquire.go:137 now scope the sentence to background-path `Acquire` tests and it is true |\n62|| Obs-1..5 | **yes** | row 6 ELOOP darwin-equivalence; B15 gains the unopenable-root, `Fchmod`, `Fsync` and leaf-`Stat` arms; B16 nested invocation (owner 1c28dz); row 23 live-member scoping; B19 caller-contract sentence |\n63|\n64|## P2 — must fix or record as a reviewed decision\n65|\n66|### P2-A. The background broker-or-refuse rule is pinned at the entry only for the fixture shapes: three realistic server-admission shapes and one realistic fallback guard walk through the committed suite\n67|\n68|SPEC §4.2 1419-1424: a background caller \"MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua\n69|broker and its **attested** AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n70|`capability_unavailable` … and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation.\" The candidate\n71|implements both halves correctly (`CheckBrokerContact` → `CheckServerAttested`; no spawn call on\n72|the path; `checkCreationAllowed` consulted by call), and the committed background miss table\n73|drives five report shapes. Four plants that admit exactly one realistic member each SURVIVED the\n74|full committed suite in both passes; each is KILLED by a reviewer probe that passes on the\n75|untouched candidate:\n76|\n77|| Row | Plant (readiness.go / acquire.go) | Member admitted under the plant | Committed suite | Probe |\n78|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n79|| R09 | before `return CheckServerAttested(report.Server, wantGeneration)`: `if RawGeneration == \"\" && !Has(realm) { return nil }` | the zero `RealmAdmission{}` server report with a live same-user generation-bound principal — the realistic nothing-reconciled state (the exact shape rev3 P2-C closed on the foreground path) | **SURVIVED ×2**, `Acquire` returns `Via: broker` for an unattested server | K02 kills |\n80|| R10 | same site: `if RawGeneration == \"\" && Has(realm) { return nil }` | rows present, generation empty, wanted generation bound | **SURVIVED ×2** | K03 kills |\n81|| R19 | same site: `if Has(\"headless_creation\") && !Has(realm) { return nil }` | decoy-only admission with a bound generation — the member the foreground entry pins via `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested` | **SURVIVED ×2** | K05 kills |\n82|| R18 | inside the miss arm, after `checkCreationAllowed` refuses: `if req.Deps.ProbeServer != nil && req.Deps.Spawn != nil { return acquireForeground(req, socket) }` | a background miss whose `Dependencies` carry the foreground probe — realistic, because the lifecycle adapter passes one shared `Dependencies` value to every caller | **SURVIVED ×2**: no committed background test arms `ProbeServer`, so the spy census (`Spawn`) never observes the fallback; the unguarded shape (`D-background-fallback`) is still killed by 11 tests | K04 kills |\n83|\n84|Why this is one class: the broker path drives exactly two server-admission shapes (`{gen, no\n85|rows}` as \"unattested server\" and `{rows, stale gen}` as \"stale server admission\") and one\n86|dependency shape (`Spawn` armed, `ProbeServer` nil). Rejection pattern (b) as stated in every\n87|brief of this task — \"if a rule is implemented TWICE (… an exported entry and its internal\n88|sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant\" — applies: the \"attested server\" rule is\n89|pinned at the helper (`TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct`) and at the foreground\n90|entry, but the broker-side wiring in `CheckBrokerContact` has no row that admits a member, and\n91|rows 27/28/31 are measured for one fixture each. The DoD lines \"negative tests that fail when the\n92|gate admits what it must reject\" and \"every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant\" are not met\n93|for the broker-side attested-server wiring; the no-fallback proof has a blind spot keyed on the\n94|sibling dependency. Production is correct today; the fix is tests plus rows:\n95|\n96|1. extend `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` with three subtests — zero\n97|   `RealmAdmission{}`, `{Admitted: realm row, RawGeneration: \"\"}`, `{Admitted: decoy only,\n98|   RawGeneration: bound}` — asserting the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6, the five typed\n99|   details, zero spawns (K02/K03/K05 are the templates), and mirror the three rows in\n100|   `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`;\n101|2. ship a narrowing row at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (the R09 shape; R10/R19 may\n102|   share the anchor) and name it under rows 27/28/36;\n103|3. arm a fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy in every background miss test (at least the two miss\n104|   tables and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`), so that a fallback through the\n105|   foreground path is visible; ship it as a second labelled additive row\n106|   (`D-background-fallback-foreground`, the R18 shape) and extend the row-31 / README sentence to\n107|   say the census arms both foreground dependencies.\n108|\n109|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n110|\n111|- **P3-A. The absence classifier's reject class is pinned at the entry for the mode and\n112|  containment members only.** Reviewer row R01 (`runtimeAbsent` widened to admit\n113|  `runtime ownership`) **SURVIVED ×2**: no committed background `Acquire` test stages foreign\n114|  ownership (the ownership gate is pinned at the helper by `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership`\n115|  on both entries, and R13 shows the verify-side wiring is killed there), so a foreign-owned leaf\n116|  on the background path would return `capability_unavailable` with the custody `*Error` as its\n117|  redacted cause — refusal-to-refusal, but the misclassification row 52 forbids (\"an unsafe leaf\n118|  keeps its custody code (top-level *Error, never the unavailable wrapper)\"). Probe K01 (background\n119|  `Acquire` + the `effectiveUID` seam → top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership`,\n120|  broker not probed, spawn 0) passes on the candidate and kills R01. Add it as\n121|  `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` under row 52, or state the ownership member as\n122|  helper-pinned only.\n123|- **P3-B. A censusable \"before\" that is false.** acquire.go:140-143 (\"Refusals precede side\n124|  effects: malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing dependencies all refuse before any directory\n125|  is created\") and results.md:61-62 (\"refuses malformed input, ambient reuse, and missing\n126|  dependencies before any side effect\"). Probe P01: a foreground request with `SessionID =\n127|  \"12345\"` **creates `<root>/tmux` and calls `ProbeServer` before** refusing `tmux_invalid_arguments\n128|  at session identity` (spawn 0). The session identity is malformed input; `acquireForeground`\n129|  validates it only inside `BuildArgv`, after `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe. Either parse the\n130|  session (`scalar.ParseUUIDv7`) at the `Acquire` entry before any side effect and add the\n131|  no-directory/no-probe assertions to `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` (row 45), or\n132|  reword both sentences to the members that are true (caller, realm details, root/name grammar,\n133|  override, collision, dependencies). Rejection pattern (f).\n134|\n135|## Observations (not findings; a sentence each in TRACEABILITY if the producer agrees)\n136|\n137|1. Probe P02: a comma inside the runtime root (`<root>/a,b`, admitted by the POSIX grammar) makes\n138|   `tmuxEnvSocket` split at the wrong comma, so a `TMUX` value naming the derived socket in the\n139|   real encoding walks past the collision gate and `Acquire` spawns. tmux(1) itself splits `TMUX`\n140|   at the first comma, so the decoding is faithful to the source of the encoding; worth a clause in\n141|   row 23/B16 (\"roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX member's encoding\").\n142|2. Probe P03: a cwd-relative spelling of the derived socket (`tmux/ax.sock` with the process cwd\n143|   at the root) walks past the cleaned-string collision gate — the same bound class as the B16\n144|   symlink alias (no path equivalence is applied); B16 could say \"symlinked or relative alias\".\n145|3. Probe P04: `Dependencies.Spawn` is inert on the background path (nil spawner + live broker\n146|   contacts) — consistent with the design; it is what makes P2-A's R18 realistic, since the shared\n147|   struct carries both foreground dependencies on a background call.\n148|4. Probe P05: a `linux` request on this darwin host commits and verifies the same unix custody on\n149|   both callers (row 14 through `Acquire`, not only `EnsureRuntimeDir`).\n150|5. Probe P06: an invalid-UTF-8 typed detail (`Generation = \"gen\\xff\"`) passes the entry's\n151|   non-empty check, is probed against the broker, and then reaches the constructor-failure arm\n152|   `backgroundUnavailable` → `tmux_invalid_arguments at realm details` (acquire.go:289-291) — an\n153|   input-reachable refusal arm with no committed test, not listed under B15 (whose members are all\n154|   seam-only). A 10,000-character remediation is admitted by the landed detail bound. Pin it with\n155|   one subtest or list it under B15 as input-reachable; note that the broker probe precedes the\n156|   refusal. While editing B15: the coverprofile also shows the commit-side leaf-`Stat` arm\n157|   (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and the `secprim.NewGuard` refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) uncovered;\n158|   both are the same unstageable/unreachable class as their listed siblings but are not named in\n159|   the list.\n160|6. The producer archive's `static-gates.log` is empty and no exit codes for the\n161|   `GOOS=windows`/`GOOS=linux` vet and test-compile gates are recorded anywhere in the archive; the\n162|   green claims live in the results prose only. Rerun here (all exit 0), so not a finding — but\n163|   record the exits next time.\n164|7. Coverage: the uncovered `background fallback` arm (acquire.go:203) is reachable only under a\n165|   weakened `checkCreationAllowed`; `N-creation-literal` exercises it under mutation, which is the\n166|   intended design (rev2 F1). Fine as is.\n167|\n168|## §M — reviewer battery (20 rows, two passes, `battery/reviewer_battery.py` in the evidence archive)\n169|\n170|Every row: anchor count verified (all 20 applied, none NOT_APPLIED, none COMPILE_FAIL), plant\n171|applied to the mutant copy, the committed suite run as shipped (full package, `-count=1 -v`, no\n172|`-run` mask), exit + raw output logged, file restored from a byte copy and re-compared, package\n173|directory hash equal before/after (`c8eb3ed00bc20f82`), `internal/` re-diffed against the\n174|candidate copy after each pass. Rows predicted SURVIVED were additionally run with\n175|`zz_review_probe_test.go` present and the named killer selected (`*.with-probe.log`).\n176|\n177|| Row | Kind | Gate (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Killer(s) |\n178|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n179|| R01-absence-admits-ownership | narrowing | `runtimeAbsent` admits `runtime ownership` (acquire.go:252) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K01 (P3-A) |\n180|| R02-absence-admits-containment | narrowing | `runtimeAbsent` admits `runtime containment` (acquire.go:252) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf |\n181|| R03-absence-admits-mode-rev4R05 | replay | `runtimeAbsent` admits `runtime mode` (acquire.go:252) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal |\n182|| R04-name-literal-lexical-site | narrowing | `\"ax-tmux\"` at the Acquire lexical step (acquire.go:151) | KILLED | — | 18 tests incl. TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath/{foreground,background} |\n183|| R05-name-literal-ensure-site | narrowing | `\"ax-tmux\"` at the foreground ensure (acquire.go:217) | KILLED | — | 8 tests incl. TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath/foreground, TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n184|| R06-name-literal-verify-site | narrowing | `\"ax-tmux\"` at the background verify (acquire.go:179) | KILLED | — | 6 tests incl. TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath/background, TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n185|| R07-absence-only-macos-rev4R14 | replay | absence remap limited to macOS (acquire.go:180) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating/{linux,wsl2} |\n186|| R08-spy-guarded-plant-top | additive | guarded `Spawn` call at the top of `acquireBackground` (acquire.go:176) | KILLED (11 top-level tests, 20 lines) | — | every background-path Acquire test that enters the function |\n187|| R09-broker-empty-admission-admits | narrowing | broker-side server wiring admits the zero admission (readiness.go:86) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K02 (P2-A) |\n188|| R10-broker-empty-generation-admits | narrowing | same site, admits rows-without-generation | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K03 (P2-A) |\n189|| R11-details-drop-generation | narrowing | typed-details gate drops the generation member (acquire.go:148) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails/generation (reroute to `dependencies`) |\n190|| R12-details-drop-brokerstate | narrowing | same, broker-state member | KILLED | — | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails/broker_state (reroute) |\n191|| R13-verify-ownership-wiring-drop | narrowing | verify side consults `verifyOwnership` and drops the verdict (runtime_unix.go:134) | KILLED | — | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership (Verify leg) |\n192|| R14-argv-drop-detached | narrowing | `-d` removed from the spawn vector (argv.go:28) | KILLED | — | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n193|| R15-argv-tail-attach | narrowing | `ax pane` → `ax attach` (argv.go:30) | KILLED | — | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket, TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n194|| R16-verify-mode-group-bits-only | replay | verify mode `!= 0700` → `&0o077 != 0` (runtime_unix.go:131) | KILLED | — | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode/{0600,0500} |\n195|| R17-commit-nofollow-drop | replay | drop `O_NOFOLLOW` on the commit Openat (runtime_unix.go:59) | KILLED | — | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf |\n196|| R18-fallback-via-foreground-guarded | additive | fallback into `acquireForeground` guarded on `ProbeServer` (acquire.go:200-202) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K04 (P2-A) |\n197|| R19-broker-decoy-admission-admits | narrowing | broker-side server wiring admits a decoy-only admission (readiness.go:86) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K05 (P2-A) |\n198|| C-reviewer-control | control | comment-only edit in readiness.go | SURVIVED | — | (must survive; proves the battery observes outcomes) |\n199|\n200|Denominator: 20 applied rows = 13 narrowing + 4 replay + 2 additive + 1 control. Of the 13\n201|narrowings, 9 KILLED by the committed suite, 4 SURVIVED (R01, R09, R10, R19), each proven real by\n202|a probe kill (production correct, suite blind). Of the 2 additives, R08 KILLED and R18 SURVIVED\n203|(probe kill). All 4 replays KILLED — the rev4 closures hold. Every KILLED row was killed by exactly\n204|the tests named above (kill lines in the raw logs).\n205|\n206|## §P — reviewer probes (11, `logs/probes-rev5.log`)\n207|\n208|K01 background + foreign ownership → top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership`,\n209|broker not probed, spawn 0 (baseline for R01); K02 broker path + zero `RealmAdmission{}` →\n210|`capability_unavailable`, spawn 0, and `CheckBrokerContact` → `server attestation` (baseline for\n211|R09); K03 broker path + admitted-without-generation → `capability_unavailable` / `server\n212|generation` (R10); K04 background miss with `ProbeServer` AND `Spawn` armed → typed unavailable,\n213|neither dependency called (R18); K05 broker path + decoy-only admission → `capability_unavailable`\n214|(R19); P01 malformed session creates the directory and probes the server before refusing (P3-B);\n215|P02 comma-root TMUX encoding walks through (obs 1); P03 relative alias walks through (obs 2); P04\n216|nil spawner on the background path contacts (obs 3); P05 linux request on both callers (obs 4);\n217|P06 invalid-UTF-8 generation reaches the constructor-failure arm after the broker probe, a 10k\n218|remediation is admitted (obs 5).\n219|\n220|## What held under attack (keep)\n221|\n222|- Dedicated-server rule per vector: override refused on all five members plus whitespace through\n223|  `Acquire` with no spawn and no directory; byte-identical, cleaned and real-encoding collisions\n224|  refused; argv gate refuses all five and the vector is pinned element-by-element (R14/R15 KILLED);\n225|  `Acquire` never reads the environment or execs; the §3.2 path is now pinned at the entry on both\n226|  callers and at all three `RuntimeDirName` sites (R04/R05/R06 KILLED).\n227|- Background rules: broker-or-refuse with the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6 and the\n228|  five typed details asserted as literals; the absent-leaf cold state returns the typed refusal on\n229|  macOS, Linux and WSL2 with no probe, no spawn and no directory (R07 KILLED); the unguarded\n230|  fallback is killed by 11 tests (R08, D-background-fallback); same-user generation-bound broker\n231|  principal at the entry (producer N-broker-uid/-generation reproduced). The residue is P2-A.\n232|- Attestation: landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` consumed through `Has` composed with the\n233|  generation equality; the foreground running arm is pinned at the entry for empty admissions;\n234|  stale, decoy and both-empty shapes refuse at the helper and on the foreground entry.\n235|- Custody: the top-level oracle now sees the wrapper (R03 KILLED; old-oracle replay SURVIVES the\n236|  same mutant); mode/containment members of the absence class pinned at the background entry;\n237|  FIFO and regular-file leaves refuse on both entries without blocking; symlink leaf refuses on\n238|  both entries (R17 KILLED); exact 0700 on both sides (R16 KILLED); ownership wiring on both sides\n239|  (R13 KILLED); read-only root, missing root, handle mismatch refuse; the real-SIGKILL crash test\n240|  converges.\n241|- Determinism: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable, 140 RUN; no real-tmux witness (B1).\n242|- Boundary: `internal/traceability` untouched; README section carries no CLI/capability claim; no\n243|  trunk drift; producer evidence archive complete and digest-verified; LOGBOOK newest-first.\n244|\n245|## Coverage ratio measured against the 58-row table\n246|\n247|**58 of 58 rows are driven as their statements are written**; the ratio is not inflated. The\n248|gaps sit beside the statements, at the member level: rows 27/28/36 (the broker-path \"attested\n249|server\" conjunct is driven for two of five admission shapes — P2-A), row 31 (the no-fallback\n250|census arms `Spawn` only — P2-A), row 52 (the custody-code half is measured for the mode and\n251|containment members, not ownership — P3-A), and acquire.go:140-143 claims a \"before\" that row 45\n252|does not measure (P3-B).\n253|\n254|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n255|\n256|1. **P2-A (tests + rows, no production change required)**: add the zero-admission,\n257|   admitted-without-generation and decoy-only server shapes to\n258|   `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` and `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`\n259|   (K02/K03/K05 in the reviewer probe file are the templates); ship a narrowing row at the\n260|   `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (R09 shape) named under rows 27/28/36; arm a fail-if-called\n261|   `ProbeServer` spy in the background miss tests and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`,\n262|   ship the R18 shape as a labelled additive row, and extend the row-31/README sentence to say the\n263|   census arms both foreground dependencies.\n264|2. **P3-A**: `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (K01 template) named under row 52, or\n265|   state the ownership member as helper-pinned only.\n266|3. **P3-B**: validate the session identity at the `Acquire` entry before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and\n267|   the probe (and assert no directory / no probe in `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession`),\n268|   or reword acquire.go:140-143 and the results sentence to the members that are true.\n269|4. Optional sentences: comma-root and relative-alias scoping under row 23/B16; the\n270|   input-reachable constructor-failure arm under B15 or a subtest; record static-gate exit codes in\n271|   the archive.\n272|5. Rerun the package suite (tmux hidden), `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, the harness\n273|   twice, and the 30-command suite; refresh results/matrix/archive; hand off as revision 6.\n274|   Everything in \"What held under attack\" needs no change — do not re-litigate it.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c54c-0ef4-78b3-96e2-4f10155428e6"},"sequence":191,"recorded_at":1780531400000377,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9"},"call_id":"call_01a0c54cce877790858fc9591a037ce4","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp results — implement-private-tmux-server-management (rev5)\n2|\n3|Rework of revision 4 after review-verdict-rev4 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no\n4|P1, two P2 classes, two P3). First leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i\n5|(production-tmux-backend, EPIC M1). The reviewer states every rev3\n6|finding (P2-A/B/C, P3-A..E, the four observations) is closed with\n7|driven evidence and stays closed, and that production behaves\n8|correctly at every point the review drove; this revision keeps all of\n9|that and changes only what the verdict grades open.\n10|\n11|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED working tree on branch\n12|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i` atop trunk `799c338` (trunk\n13|unmoved since rev4; no refresh, no rebase, no commit, no merge by this\n14|run). `git status` shows only `internal/tmuxserver/`, `README.md`,\n15|`LOGBOOK.md`.\n16|\n17|Normative source: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n18|§3.2 platform paths (lines 765-813: the dedicated socket\n19|`<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root) and §4.2 tmux\n20|backend (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220), and\n21|§4.E (1309) as context, plus §4.3 (1458) and §4.4 for the Windows\n22|and broker rules. All clause citations name the pinned file, never\n23|the network, never v0.5.0.\n24|\n25|## Finding-by-finding table (verdict -> change -> test that fails without it -> evidence)\n26|\n27|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n28||---|---|---|---|\n29|| P2-A custody oracle looks through the wrapper; no narrowing admits a member the absence classifier must reject | `requireLocalError` now asserts the TOP-LEVEL `*Error` dynamic type plus no reachable `*axerror.Error` (the wrapper IS the observable refusal: the cause is redacted off the wire). Shipped `N-absence-remap-widen` in the reviewer's R05 shape (`runtimeAbsent` admitting `runtime mode`); kept `N-background-absence-remap` (rewritten to the platform conjunct after the `Request.Name` deletion) for the reject direction. Re-ran every custody row after the oracle change: none only passed because of the old helper | `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal` (a widened 0755 leaf maps to `capability_unavailable` under the mutant; the top-level assertion reddens). Proven load-bearing: the row SURVIVES under the old helper (reproduces R05) and KILLS under the fixed one | `harness-pass1/N-absence-remap-widen.log`, `harness-pass1/N-background-absence-remap.log` (+ pass 2), `plant-replays/N-absence-remap-widen.log` + `oracle-replay-old-verdict.log` (old-oracle SURVIVED replay) |\n30|| P2-B `Request.Name` re-opens the §3.2 divergence per call; the spec path pinned at the constants, not the entry | `Request.Name` DELETED: `Acquire` always passes `RuntimeDirName`, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths. `EnsureRuntimeDir`/`VerifyRuntimeDir` keep their `name` parameter for the grammar rows. New `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` through `Acquire` for foreground and background; rows 16/56 name it. The P01 probe is unstageable (the field does not exist) and R11 inapplicable | `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` (foreground, background subtests; any caller-selectable leaf or renamed constant reddens) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `internal/tmuxserver/acquire.go` |\n31|| P3-A absence remap pinned on the macOS axis only | `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` now drives macos, linux, and wsl2 subtests (the cold state is identical: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is tmpfs); named under row 52 | The linux/wsl2 subtests (the reviewer's R14 shape fails on both firsthand, macos still maps) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `R14-replay.log` (R14 plant: macos PASS, linux/wsl2 FAIL) |\n32|| P3-B censusable \"every background test arms a spy\" is false (7 of 11) | Armed the spy in all four (`TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid`, `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf`, the background half of `TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies`, the background iteration of `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform`, each asserting zero calls) and scoped the README/`acquire.go` sentence to background-path `Acquire` tests. Mechanical census: 12/12 armed (incl. the new background subtest) | The four tests' new zero-call assertions (a guarded `D-background-fallback`-shaped plant is visible to all of them) | `pkg-tests-v.log` |\n33|| Obs R03/ELOOP, unopenable root, Fchmod/Fsync/Stat arms, nested invocation, vacuous members | One-sentence TRACEABILITY entries: ELOOP darwin-equivalence under row 6 (reasoned, not run); the 0000-root arm and the `Fchmod`/`Fsync`/leaf-`Stat` arms under B15 as error-arm rows; the nested-invocation over-strict refusal under B16 (owner TASK-260830-1c28dz); the live-member scoping (`TMUXEnv`/`InheritedSocket` only) under row 23; the `localstore`-root caller contract stated as undriven under B19 | — (bounds/prose, no behavior) | `TRACEABILITY.md` rows 6/23, B15/B16/B19 |\n34|\n35|Kept untouched per the verdict: the dedicated-server rule per vector,\n36|the background broker-or-refuse wiring with the literal\n37|`capability_unavailable` and typed details, the no-fallback rule along\n38|the caller/credential/platform axes, the landed-admission attestation\n39|composition (incl. the admission-empty Running pins), the custody\n40|gates that held under attack (FIFO/symlink/mode/UID/handle-mismatch\n41|refusals, the explicit `Fchmod`, the real-SIGKILL crash test), the\n42|determinism design (no real-tmux witness), and the\n43|`internal/traceability` boundary.\n44|\n45|## Deliverable (rev5 shape)\n46|\n47|`internal/tmuxserver`, composing the landed owners (never forked):\n48|\n49|- (1) Runtime custody: `EnsureRuntimeDir` / `VerifyRuntimeDir` with\n50|  three independent gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership).\n51|  Foreground acquisition ensures idempotently; background acquisition\n52|  verifies the existing directory and never creates it. Absence\n53|  (`ENOENT`) carries its own detail; the missing-root mapping is one\n54|  shared classifier.\n55|- (2) Dedicated socket: `SocketPath` / `ResolveSocket` derive\n56|  `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` — the spec's path — and refuse overrides and\n57|  ambient collisions on all five members, with the TMUX member\n58|  compared in its real encoding and unclean spellings cleaned\n59|  (symlink aliases bound). The runtime leaf is not an `Acquire`\n60|  input: the entry always passes `RuntimeDirName`.\n61|- (3) Acquisition: `Acquire` refuses malformed input, ambient reuse,\n62|  and missing dependencies before any side effect. Foreground attaches\n63|  or spawns (a running server never spawns, even with empty\n64|  admission); background brokers-or-refuses with the typed\n65|  `capability_unavailable` — including the absent-leaf cold state on\n66|  macOS, Linux, and WSL2 — and no fallback (the miss path consults\n67|  the creation gate by call; every background-path `Acquire` test arms\n68|  a zero-call spy).\n69|- (4) Readiness: `CheckServerAttested` / `CheckBrokerContact` decide\n70|  the landed admission (`Admitted.Has(realm)` + generation equality)\n71|  over a typed same-user generation-bound broker principal. A stale\n72|  admission — the replayed-cached shape — refuses on both paths.\n73|- (5) Spawn argv: `Build