 below cover\n22|deliberately unclaimed surfaces, not undriven rows.\n23|\n24|No test in this package starts a tmux process: every broker, server,\n25|and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies, and the\n26|suite passes with no tmux installed. No row has a real-tmux witness;\n27|that is the determinism design, not a gap (bound B1).\n28|\n29|Attestation authority: the sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n30|verification, liveness, and expiry verdict is the landed\n31|internal/terminalbackend Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission,\n32|consumed here as an Admitted set composed only with the generation\n33|equality the wrapper owner (internal/axpane checkRealm) already\n34|enforces. This leaf decides membership plus generation binding and\n35|re-decides nothing the admission proves.\n36|\n37|## Runtime custody (Sections 4.2, 4.E)\n38|\n39|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n40||---|--------|-----------|------|\n41|| 1 | Ensure creates the owner-only 0700 directory, explicitly under a restrictive umask | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirCreatesOwnerOnly, TestEnsureRuntimeDirEnforcesModeUnderRestrictiveUmask |\n42|| 2 | Re-ensure is idempotent and verifies mode | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent |\n43|| 3 | Compliant directory verifies | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirAdmitsCompliant |\n44|| 4 | Widened (0755) and narrower (0600/0500) modes refuse on ensure and verify, never silently repaired | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode, TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode |\n45|| 5 | Non-directory leaf refuses on commit and verify; the verify open carries no O_NONBLOCK by decision — FIFO refusal relies on O_DIRECTORY failing fast, pinned by the deadline test | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go), Acquire (acquire.go, background) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf (regular file, FIFO under deadline), TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf |\n46|| 6 | Symlink leaf refuses on commit and verify. On darwin the verify-side ELOOP arm is unreachable — openat(O_NOFOLLOW&#124;O_DIRECTORY) on a symlink leaf returns ENOTDIR — while on Linux the same open returns ELOOP, mapped to containment; reasoned, not run, since the configured suite is darwin-only | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf |\n47|| 7 | Foreign ownership refuses on ensure and verify | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (ownership_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership |\n48|| 8 | Handle/path mismatch refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesHandleMismatch |\n49|| 9 | Symlinked root refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkRoot |\n50|| 10 | Relative, empty, parent, and missing roots refuse invalid (runtime root), the same code verify reports (row 13) | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadRoots (4 subtests) |\n51|| 11 | Empty, dot, parent, nested, absolute, and NUL names refuse | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadNames (6 subtests) |\n52|| 12 | Unknown platform refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadPlatform |\n53|| 13 | Verify refuses absence (runtime absent) and a missing root (runtime root, aligned with the commit side via the shared classifier) without creating | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesAbsence, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesBadLexical, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesMissingRoot |\n54|| 14 | Linux and WSL2 share the unix custody discipline | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestLinuxAndWSL2ShareUnixCustody |\n55|| 15 | Windows platform refuses on every host; no tmux directory exists on Windows | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost, TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform |\n56|| 57 | Commit-phase filesystem failure (unwritable root) refuses the commit detail instead of being mistaken for an existing leaf | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot |\n57|\n58|## Socket path and runtime root (Section 3.2)\n59|\n60|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n61||---|--------|-----------|------|\n62|| 56 | Dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root (macOS: per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), resolved by the landed localstore layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity. The runtime leaf is not an Acquire input — the entry always passes RuntimeDirName, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths. The parent's verifiable custody (owned, 0700, component-verified without following a symlink) is rows 1-15; root creation custody is the localstore layout owner's (B19) and provenance is unclaimed (B20) | SocketPath (socket.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n63|\n64|## Dedicated socket and ambient non-use (Section 4.2)\n65|\n66|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n67||---|--------|-----------|------|\n68|| 16 | Socket derives only from the runtime directory, as `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` with both leaves asserted as spec literals; the Acquire outcome socket equals `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths | SocketPath (socket.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n69|| 17 | Resolution returns the derived socket under hostile ambient on all five members | ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n70|| 18 | Ambient observation records without using, including nil lookup | ObserveAmbient (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, TestObserveAmbientNilLookupKeepsOutOfBand |\n71|| 19 | TMUX environment value as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/environment_variable |\n72|| 20 | Inherited socket as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/inherited_socket |\n73|| 21 | Default path as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/default_path |\n74|| 22 | Conventional name as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/conventional_name |\n75|| 23 | Ambient value colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member, byte-identical and unclean (`/./`, `//`) spellings alike, and the TMUX member in the real `<socket>,<pid>,<index>` encoding. Only TMUXEnv and InheritedSocket can name the derived socket in real tmux semantics (TMUX_TMPDIR is a directory; DefaultPath/ConventionalName end in `default`, never `ax.sock`) — the other three members pin defence-in-depth shapes, not live vectors | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpellings (2 subtests), TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpelling, TestResolveSocketRefusesTMUXEnvRealEncoding, TestAcquireRefusesTMUXEnvCollisionRealEncoding |\n76|| 55 | TMUX_TMPDIR value as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/tmux_tmpdir |\n77|| 58 | Whitespace-only override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/whitespace_only, TestResolveSocketRefusesEveryOverrideVector/whitespace_only |\n78|\n79|## Background broker-or-refuse (Section 4.2)\n80|\n81|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n82||---|--------|-----------|------|\n83|| 24 | Authenticated same-user broker plus generation-bound attested server contacts on macOS, with no spawn and no argv | Acquire (acquire.go) via CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n84|| 25 | No broker returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/no_broker |\n85|| 26 | Foreign-user broker returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n86|| 27 | Unattested server returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/unattested_server |\n87|| 28 | Stale-generation admission returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/generation-unbound_principal |\n88|| 29 | Linux miss also returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback |\n89|| 30 | Broker probe failure passes through as unknown, never unavailable, with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n90|| 31 | Creation gate refuses the background caller; the miss path enforces it by call | checkCreationAllowed via Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable (kill path of N-creation-literal) |\n91|\n92|## Readiness non-authorization (Sections 4.2, 4.D)\n93|\n94|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n95||---|--------|-----------|------|\n96|| 32 | A stale admission replayed on a broker miss still returns the typed capability_unavailable: cached proof authorizes nothing | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission |\n97|| 33 | A stale admission fakes no running attested server on the foreground path | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission |\n98|| 34 | Bound admitted row admits | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedAdmitsBound |\n99|| 35 | Missing realm row refuses, including a decoy capability | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct (no admission rows, decoy capability only), TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested |\n100|| 36 | Wrong-generation admission refuses, including the both-empty pair | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct (stale generation admission, both generations empty), TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission |\n101|| 37 | Foreign-user broker principal refuses | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact (no broker, foreign-user broker), TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n102|| 38 | Generation-unbound broker principal refuses, including the both-empty pair | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact (generation-unbound, empty and both-empty principal), TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/generation-unbound_principal |\n103|| 39 | Complete broker report admits | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactAdmitsLiveReport |\n104|\n105|## Foreground acquisition (Section 4.2)\n106|\n107|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n108||---|--------|-----------|------|\n109|| 40 | Absent server spawns dedicated with exact -S argv disjoint from every ambient vector and the ax pane tail | Acquire (acquire.go) via BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n110|| 41 | Running attested server attaches with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested |\n111|| 42 | Running unattested server refuses with no spawn and no repair, including a running server with zero admission rows and one with an empty generation | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested, TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningWithEmptyAdmission, TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningWithEmptyGeneration |\n112|| 43 | Server probe failure passes through as unknown with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n113|| 44 | Spawn failure reports with exactly one attempt and no fallback | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnFailureReportsWithoutFallback |\n114|| 45 | Malformed session refuses before any spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) via BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession |\n115|\n116|## Spawn argv (Sections 4.2, 4.C)\n117|\n118|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n119||---|--------|-----------|------|\n120|| 46 | Spawn vector is exactly tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n121|| 47 | All five ambient sockets refuse | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket (5 subtests) |\n122|| 48 | Malformed sessions refuse the landed UUIDv7 wiring | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesMalformedSession |\n123|\n124|## Input validation (Sections 4.2, 15.3)\n125|\n126|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n127||---|--------|-----------|------|\n128|| 49 | Unknown caller refuses | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesUnknownCaller |\n129|| 50 | Missing generation, broker state, and remediation each refuse | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails (3 subtests) |\n130|| 51 | Missing dependencies refuse on every nil shape | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies, TestAcquireBackgroundNilBrokerWithSpawnRefuses, TestAcquireForegroundNilSpawnWithProbeRefuses |\n131|| 52 | Foreground acquisition ensures the runtime directory idempotently; background verifies without creating — an absent leaf on macOS, Linux, and WSL2 returns the typed capability_unavailable, a missing root refuses invalid, an unsafe leaf keeps its custody code (top-level *Error, never the unavailable wrapper) | Acquire (acquire.go) via EnsureRuntimeDir/VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently, TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating (macos, linux, wsl2), TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid, TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal, TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf |\n132|\n133|## Crash and idempotency (Sections 4.2, 4.E)\n134|\n135|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n136||---|--------|-----------|------|\n137|| 53 | Real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync leaves a retry that converges to the one verified directory | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates |\n138|| 54 | Spawn-then-retry attaches to the one server with exactly one spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry |\n139|\n140|## Mutation battery\n141|\n142|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`:\n143|55 narrowing rows KILLED, 1 supplementary additive row KILLED\n144|(D-background-fallback, labeled), 1 harmless control SURVIVED, on two\n145|full passes with identical verdicts and one raw log per plant per run.\n146|Row N-deps-foreground kills by panic: the admitted request calls the\n147|nil spawner and the panic fails the test. Rows N-verify-absence-detail\n148|(background leg), N-broker-empty-generation, and N-commit-eacces-as-exist\n149|kill by reroute to a neighboring refusal, disclosed in their row notes.\n150|N-absence-remap-widen kills through the top-level custody oracle:\n151|under the errors.As helper the row survives (the reviewer's R05),\n152|under the top-level assertion it kills. No token-preserving\n153|source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text, and the\n154|harness executes the behavioral suite (bound B4). The reviewers'\n155|error-arm plants (stat-failure arms flipped to fail-open, the\n156|unreachable guard arm, the unopenable-root arm) are reported as\n157|error-arm rows under bound B15, never counted among the narrowing\n158|rows.\n159|\n160|## Stated bounds\n161|\n162|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n163|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n164|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n165|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n166|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n167|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n168|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n169|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n170|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n171|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n172|  panic kill.\n173|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n174|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n175|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n176|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n177|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n178|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n179|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n180|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n181|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n182|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n183|  conformance matrix only.\n184|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n185|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n186|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n187|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n188|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n189|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n190|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n191|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n192|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n193|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n194|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n195|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n196|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n197|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n198|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n199|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n200|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir;\n201|  through Acquire the directory always names a created directory.\n202|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n203|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n204|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n205|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n206|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n207|- B14 The battery and the read-only-root test assume a non-root test\n208|  user: N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit\n209|  chmod, so under root it is equivalent to the original and survives,\n210|  and TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot stages a genuine EACCES\n211|  only when permission bits bind the test user. The reviewer's\n212|  same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.\n213|- B15 Unmeasured fail-closed stat arms, no seam: handleBoundToPath's\n214|  two stat-failure arms (runtime.go) and verifyOwnership's !ok arm\n215|  (ownership_unix.go) fail closed by code and are prose only by test —\n216|  no test can stage a Stat failure on an open directory handle, or a\n217|  stat without ownership metadata on unix, without a seam. The\n218|  guard.Resolve refusal arm (runtime.go) is unreachable through the\n219|  name grammar: every input the guard would refuse is refused earlier\n220|  by scalar, so the fail-open plant survives by construction. The same\n221|  unstageable class covers the commit-side Fchmod and parent-Fsync\n222|  failure arms and the verify-side leaf-Stat failure arm\n223|  (runtime_unix.go): no committed test stages those failures. An\n224|  unopenable (0000) root reports `runtime containment` on both entries\n225|  with no committed test staging it — classifying EACCES as missing\n226|  would reroute it to `runtime root`, refusal-to-refusal. Reported\n227|  as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n228|- B16 The collision gate compares cleaned byte strings: an ambient\n229|  value naming the derived socket through a symlinked alias of the\n230|  root walks past it (realpath equivalence is not applied). The spec\n231|  rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never selected from an\n232|  ambient value — so this bounds only the package-local\n233|  defense-in-depth claim. An `ax` invocation from inside its own AX\n234|  pane refuses `ambient collision` when the caller populates Ambient\n235|  from the process environment (TMUX=`<derived>`,pid,idx in the real\n236|  encoding): over-strict rather than over-permissive, and the caller\n237|  owns what it observes — the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz\n238|  decides the nested-invocation rule deliberately.\n239|- B17 The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on\n240|  a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This\n241|  matches the landed hosttrust custody precedent\n242|  (internal/hosttrust/custody_unix.go platformModeOK: Perm() == mode),\n243|  so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n244|- B18 The derived socket path is not checked against the platform\n245|  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep runtime root surfaces\n246|  as a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter, owned by\n247|  TASK-260830-1c28dz.\n248|- B19 The Runtime IPC root's own mode and ownership are not gated in\n249|  this leaf: the root arrives as the caller-supplied\n250|  localstore-resolved PathRuntime value, its creation-time custody is\n251|  the localstore layout owner's, and the SPEC 810-812\n252|  before-bind/connect rejection of an unsafe path, parent, or ancestor\n253|  is the lifecycle bind step's (TASK-260830-1c28dz), which is the step\n254|  that binds. This leaf pins the root handle (no-follow open plus\n255|  handle/path binding) and commits the leaf relative to it; a\n256|  world-writable root is admitted here and refused at bind. That the\n257|  root value is the landed localstore PathRuntime is a contract\n258|  statement about the caller, not a driven fact: no test composes\n259|  localstore with Acquire.\n260|- B20 Whether the runtime leaf was created by AX is indistinguishable\n261|  after the fact: any same-user 0700 directory under an admitted name\n262|  is accepted. The verifiable properties — mode, ownership, kind,\n263|  containment — are gated (rows 1-15); provenance is not claimed.\n264|- B21 No broker is modelled as the zero BrokerReport, whose\n265|  Principal.UID is 0: for a non-root process the absent broker\n266|  refuses on the authentication arm, while under a root process the\n267|  same-user arm passes and refusal comes from the generation arm.\n268|  The broker-path outcome socket binding is the generation equality\n269|  only — BrokerReport carries no socket of its own.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
