{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c71d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c54c-0ef4-78b3-96e2-4f10155428e6"},"sequence":489,"recorded_at":1780531400000973,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c54e-b152-7f31-8750-5863524393f9"},"task_id":"01a0c54e-b152-7f31-8750-5863524393f9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c54e-b152-7f31-8750-5863524393f9","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-12-1\",\n  \"command\": \"WT=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree\\ngrep -n \\\"effectiveUID\\\" \\\"$WT/internal/tmuxserver/runtime_test.go\\\" | head\\necho ===\\ngrep -n \\\"tmuxserver\\\\|tmux-server\\\\|Private tmux\\\" \\\"$WT/README.md\\\" | head\\necho ===\\nhead -60 \\\"$WT/LOGBOOK.md\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Check seam usage, README, LOGBOOK\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"185:\\tprevious := effectiveUID\\n186:\\teffectiveUID = func() int { return previous() + 100000 }\\n187:\\tdefer func() { effectiveUID = previous }()\\n===\\n2329:## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\\n2331:[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\\n2368:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n2369:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n2376:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n2387:[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev4 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, two P2, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev3 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove). P2-A: `requireLocalError` now asserts the TOP-LEVEL `*Error` (plus no reachable `*axerror.Error`), because `errors.As` looked through the `capability_unavailable` wrapper whose cause is redacted off the wire — the new `N-absence-remap-widen` (the reviewer's R05 shape: `runtimeAbsent` admitting `runtime mode`) SURVIVES under the old helper and KILLS under the fixed one, proven by replay; `N-background-absence-remap` kept for the other direction. Re-ran every custody row after the oracle change: none only passed because of the old helper.\\n- P2-B: `Request.Name` is DELETED — the acquisition entry always passes `RuntimeDirName`, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths with no per-call spelling that can re-open the `§3.2` divergence (the reviewer's P01 probe is unstageable: the field does not exist; R11 is inapplicable). `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` through `Acquire` for foreground and background, named under rows 16/56. P3-A: `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` now drives macos/linux/wsl2 subtests (the reviewer's R14 shape fails on linux+wsl2 firsthand, named under row 52). P3-B: the four unarmed background tests now arm the spy, and the README/`acquire.go` sentence is scoped to background-path `Acquire` tests — mechanical census: 12/12 armed.\\n- Observations: row 6 states the ELOOP darwin-equivalence (reasoned, not run); B15 gains the unopenable-root arm and the `Fchmod`/`Fsync`/leaf-`Stat` arms; B16 states the nested-invocation over-strict refusal (owner: TASK-260830-1c28dz); row 23 scopes the live collision members to `TMUXEnv`/`InheritedSocket`; B19 states the `localstore`-root caller contract as undriven.\\n- Battery: 55 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 57/57 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev5). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev4 — Private tmux server management rework (spec socket path, background absence code, Running-arm entry pins, TMUX encoding, bounds)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev3 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, three P2, five P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev2 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept). P2-A: the derived path is now the path the spec mandates — `RuntimeDirName = \\\"tmux\\\"`, `SocketName = \\\"ax.sock\\\"`, both asserted as spec literals plus the joined `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` in `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir`; `Request.Root` is documented as the Runtime IPC root resolved by the landed `localstore` layout as `PathRuntime` (no second resolution), with a §3.2 row 56 in TRACEABILITY and the matrix. P2-B+P3-B: the verify side distinguishes `ENOENT` (new `runtime absent` detail) from `ENOTDIR`/`ELOOP`/other, the missing-root code is aligned across commit and verify through one shared classifier, and the background path maps an absent leaf to the typed `capability_unavailable` with no probe, no spawn, and no directory write — while an existing-but-unsafe leaf keeps its custody code (`TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` rewritten, `TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid` added, narrowings `N-verify-absence-detail` / `N-background-absence-remap` / `N-root-missing-classify`).\\n- P2-C: the foreground Running arm is pinned at the entry for admission-empty servers — `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningWithEmptyAdmission` / `...WithEmptyGeneration` plus `N-running-empty-admission` / `N-running-empty-generation` (the reviewer's R01/R02 shapes, killing by a second spawn). P3-A: the TMUX collision member compares the socket component of the real `<socket>,<pid>,<index>` encoding at both levels (`N-collision-tmuxenv-encoding` drops the split). P3-C: root custody and \\\"AX-created\\\" stated as bounds B19/B20 with named owners (localstore layout creation, lifecycle bind step TASK-260830-1c28dz). P3-D: the `environ`-grammar comment corrected to what the code does and the always-nil `ObserveAmbient` error return dropped. P3-E: read-only-root (`runtime commit`, `N-commit-eacces-as-exist`, non-root bound) and whitespace-override rows added (`N-override-whitespace`, new rows 57/58). Observations: B15 gains the unreachable guard arm, B21 states the zero-UID broker model and generation-only socket binding, the `AfterMkdir` comment now says created-or-present.\\n- Battery: 54 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 56/56 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev4). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev3 — Private tmux server management rework (verify-side non-directory pin, both-empty arms, narrower-mode pin, cleaned collision)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2, five P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev1 finding stays closed). P2-A: the verify-side non-directory refusal is now pinned on the entry the background path uses — `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (0700 regular file admitted outright under the mutant; FIFO under a 5s deadline so the no-hang property pins too) plus `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` through the background entry, with harness row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` (kill signature: err-nil on both entries, 5s FIFO stall). Deliberate gate decision: the verify `Openat` carries no `O_NONBLOCK` — FIFO refusal relies on `O_DIRECTORY` failing fast, symmetric with the commit side, stated in TRACEABILITY row 5.\\n- P3-A: both-empty generation rows in both readiness tables plus `N-realm-empty-want` / `N-broker-empty-generation` (the broker row kills by reroute to the server-generation detail, disclosed in its note). P3-B: the narrower side of \\\"exactly 0700\\\" pinned — a pre-existing 0600/0500 leaf refuses `runtime mode` on both entries (`TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode`, `N-mode-narrower-create/verify`), so the exact-0700 prose stands as written. P3-C: the collision gate compares `filepath.Clean` spellings (one production-line change; `/./` and `//` aliases refused at `ResolveSocket` and through `Acquire`, `N-collision-unclean` drops `Clean`; symlink aliases bound B16). P3-D: the rev1 LOGBOOK block folded into rev2 (F1-F3 preserved, stale bullets replaced with a SUPERSEDED pointer). P3-E: stat-failure arms stated as bound B15 (error-arm rows, never counted as narrowings). Observations: import-census no-fallback bound under B9, Perm-only mode bound B17 (hosttrust precedent), `sun_path` bound B18 owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz.\\n- Battery: 46 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 48/48 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 55 of 55 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev3; row 5 names both entries, rows 4/23/36/38 name the new pins). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in 6 bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 64 pass / 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev2 — Private tmux server management rework (P1 attestation fork + Windows vet, 9 surviving narrowings)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev1 (CHANGES REQUESTED: 2 P1, 4 P2, 4 P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh). P1-A: `runtime_test.go` now carries `//go:build !windows` (it reassigns the unix-only `effectiveUID` seam and uses `syscall.Umask`); `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` is green (exit 0, run firsthand). P1-B: the forked `LiveAttestation`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`/`BrokerStatus` model is DELETED — `RealmAdmission` consumes the landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` verdict composed only with the `RawGeneration == Generation` equality `axpane.checkRealm` enforces, and the broker principal is a typed same-user UID plus generation-bound generation (no bare boolean); `Request.Hint`/`Cached`/`NeedsCredentials` are deleted with no replacement fields. The three reviewer holes now refuse through `Acquire`: wrong-generation foreground attach, wrong-generation broker contact, and a stale admission (the replayed-cached shape) on both paths.\\n- P2-A: nine surviving narrowings closed with committed killers + shipped rows — `Acquire` commit-phase refusal (`TestAcquireForegroundStagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-commit-refusal), background verify wiring (`TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-verify-refusal), verify-side symlink leaf (N-containment-symlink-verify), `TMUX_TMPDIR` override as the fifth vector (row 55, N-override-tmpdir), per-member collisions through `Acquire` (N-collision ×4), TMUX-env argv member (N-argv-tmuxenv), umask-0177 create proving the explicit `Fchmod` (N-fchmod-umask); the unreachable `ObserveAmbient` vocabulary arm is deleted. P2-B: `PlatformWindows` refuses at the lexical gate on every host (`tmux_invalid_arguments`); the Windows commit/verify arms are refusal stubs and the tripwire is deleted. P2-C: the decision-core-only split is a stated bound (B9, exec/probe adapters + socket crash evidence owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz) and the \\\"production wires\\\" sentence is deleted. P2-D: background acquisition verifies instead of ensuring (no durable write on the aut