rsize/edge tests, sessadapter owner); cases 144→145; digest re-derived `4bd01143…` gate-computed; README prose fixed (7.8 bound to sessadapter, Nine cases, admissions list, 10.2 union note).\\n- REV2 EVIDENCE: 62 narrowing + 2 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; the six re-anchorable reviewer plants (R1,R2,R5,R6,R7,R8 shapes) KILLED firsthand by the new tests. AC: 38 of 38 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev2).\\n- REV3 CORRECTION (rework of review RUN-260918-a4ffef, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): the REV2 sentence \\\"the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate\\\" was FALSE — the struct decode matched member names case-insensitively and took the last match, so a case-folded alias overrode the claimed value while the strict map admitted it as a distinct extra. The second decoder is DELETED: `parseNativeLine` now reads the six claimed envelope members from the strict map by exact name (`json.Unmarshal(members[name], ...)` + `Body = members[\\\"body\\\"]`), and no lenient re-read of the envelope remains anywhere after the strict gate (verified by grep: the only struct decode is gone; every other `Unmarshal` reads a strict-map member or a sealed manifest map by exact key).\\n- REV3 (same run): P1-b CLOSED — `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers` pins all six alias axes through `Normalize` (kind in both document orders, origin/authority, protection/promotion refusal, body/content, evidence identity, actor/attribution refusal) plus an unrelated-extra control; six `N-alias-*` narrowings each restore the case-folded read for exactly one member and all KILLED. P2-d CLOSED — positive `reasoning_summary` row (`TestNormalizeReasoningSummaryProjectsInternal`) + routing-swap narrowing. P3-m capture status asserted for every emitted kind (`TestNormalizeCaptureStatusExactForEveryKind` + partial-stamp narrowing); P3-n last-wins pinned by two native instructions (`TestNormalizeLastNativeInstructionWins` + fold-first narrowing); P3-o external kind pinned (`TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` + kind narrowing, and the reviewer-exact R7 swap KILLED firsthand); P3-p unknown-type-without-body refusal row + required-member narrowing (reviewer R1 shape); P3-q `text:null` stated as a bound (seals empty inline content, pinned) with `ciphertext:null` noted harmless; P3-r `N-pending-aborted` relabelled add-arm and the shared-site `N-strict-*` rows disclosed as one gate/two call sites (harness + TRACEABILITY + matrix + results); P3-s per-edge bound text now names `native_type` (reviewer R2 re-run firsthand: SURVIVED, inside the bound). Five prose sites corrected (`native.go` comments, TRACEABILITY rows, README exact-name sentence, this entry, results).\\n- REV3 EVIDENCE: 72 narrowing + 3 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; reviewer R1/R4/R5/R6 shapes adopted as shipped narrowings, R7 adopted as a condition narrowing with the exact swap also KILLED firsthand, R3 still KILLED (untouched line). AC: 45 of 45 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev3).\\n- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260918-d009f2, CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1; the rev2 rework is CLOSED AT THE CLASS per the verdict's Section 0 — kept untouched): P2-e CLOSED — `TestNormalizeMultiRecordRefsResolveAtAssertedOffsets` resolves EVERY event's `RawRefs[0]` against its own line with offsets asserted (`0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2`, multibyte first line), plus labelled behaviour-swap `N-offset-newline`; the reviewer's `RV-offset-line-number` and `RV-evidence-offset-second-line` shapes KILLED firsthand by the new row. P3-u/z pinned as bounds (`TestNormalizeNullOptionalBoolsDecodeAsFalse`, `TestNormalizeUnknownTypeNullBodyProjectsOpaque`); P3-v rows shipped (`body_text_number`, `body_live_attestation_string`, `body_missing_text` + 3 narrowings, the required gate pinned by its message); P3-w low edge pinned (`empty_directive` + `N-directive-empty`); P3-x `doc.go` nine→ten; P3-y declined-cosmetic with rationale (uniform member+line error shape is AC-pinned; the clonebundle helper wording at `session.go:527` is accepted sibling production, behavior verified correct); P3-aa MANIFEST self-entry dropped. No production change: test-plus-matrix only.\\n- REV4 REFRESH: trunk moved `c3aae73`→`42d5a95` (sibling STORY-260830-ptxkqe landed) before this run, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `42d5a95`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay for both checkpoints); the audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/fencing`, `internal/terminalbackend`) and MERGED the five co-owned files (LOGBOOK newest-first, README figures+prose, ownership registry 152 cases/74 rows with every trunk row intact, the four pin tests); `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` re-derived via the gate as `614eb55d…` (command+output in results); `tracecheck` green `70/574` with `--section 7.8`/`10.2` admitted. AC: 47 of 47 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev4).\\n- REV5 (rework of review RUN-260918-492d65, CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1; the ENTIRE rev3 rework is CLOSED and the refresh was a verified MERGE per the verdict's Section 0 — kept untouched; trunk unmoved at `42d5a95`, no refresh): P2-f CLOSED — the AC-named scale far edges are driven, not delegated: 65-parent / 1025-head / 1025-actor / 1000001-event-ID refusal rows at build AND decode in `internal/clonebundle` (each asserting code + message; otherwise-valid inputs so every build-side widening kills by admission), 8 widening narrowings (one per build/decode site, incl. the decode-actors row's missing narrowing), matrix section D and `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md` citing rows by name. P3-bb unterminated multi-line tail row (last event + offset asserted)