{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c723","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c54c-0ef4-78b3-96e2-4f10155428e6"},"sequence":492,"recorded_at":1780531400000979,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9"},"call_id":"call_01a0c54ea71c750ba40719dcd1f2a71f","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-12-1\",\n  \"command\": \"WT=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree\\ngrep -n \\\"effectiveUID\\\" \\\"$WT/internal/tmuxserver/runtime_test.go\\\" | head\\necho ===\\ngrep -n \\\"tmuxserver\\\\|tmux-server\\\\|Private tmux\\\" \\\"$WT/README.md\\\" | head\\necho ===\\nhead -60 \\\"$WT/LOGBOOK.md\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Check seam usage, README, LOGBOOK\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"185:\\tprevious := effectiveUID\\n186:\\teffectiveUID = func() int { return previous() + 100000 }\\n187:\\tdefer func() { effectiveUID = previous }()\\n===\\n2329:## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\\n2331:[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\\n2368:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n2369:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n2376:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n2387:[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev4 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, two P2, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev3 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove). P2-A: `requireLocalError` now asserts the TOP-LEVEL `*Error` (plus no reachable `*axerror.Error`), because `errors.As` looked through the `capability_unavailable` wrapper whose cause is redacted off the wire — the new `N-absence-remap-widen` (the reviewer's R05 shape: `runtimeAbsent` admitting `runtime mode`) SURVIVES under the old helper and KILLS under the fixed one, proven by replay; `N-background-absence-remap` kept for the other direction. Re-ran every custody row after the oracle change: none only passed because of the old helper.\\n- P2-B: `Request.Name` is DELETED — the acquisition entry always passes `RuntimeDirName`, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths with no per-call spelling that can re-open the `§3.2` divergence (the reviewer's P01 probe is unstageable: the field does not exist; R11 is inapplicable). `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` through `Acquire` for foreground and background, named under rows 16/56. P3-A: `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` now drives macos/linux/wsl2 subtests (the reviewer's R14 shape fails on linux+wsl2 firsthand, named under row 52). P3-B: the four unarmed background tests now arm the spy, and the README/`acquire.go` sentence is scoped to background-path `Acquire` tests — mechanical census: 12/12 armed.\\n- Observations: row 6 states the ELOOP darwin-equivalence (reasoned, not run); B15 gains the unopenable-root arm and the `Fchmod`/`Fsync`/leaf-`Stat` arms; B16 states the nested-invocation over-strict refusal (owner: TASK-260830-1c28dz); row 23 scopes the live collision members to `TMUXEnv`/`InheritedSocket`; B19 states the `localstore`-root caller contract as undriven.\\n- Battery: 55 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 57/57 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev5). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev4 — Private tmux server management rework (spec socket path, background absence code, Running-arm entry pins, TMUX encoding, bounds)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev3 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, three P2, five P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev2 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept). P2-A: the derived path is now the path the spec mandates — `RuntimeDirName = \\\"tmux\\\"`, `SocketName = \\\"ax.sock\\\"`, both asserted as spec literals plus the joined `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` in `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir`; `Request.Root` is documented as the Runtime IPC root resolved by the landed `localstore` layout as `PathRuntime` (no second resolution), with a §3.2 row 56 in TRACEABILITY and the matrix. P2-B+P3-B: the verify side distinguishes `ENOENT` (new `runtime absent` detail) from `ENOTDIR`/`ELOOP`/other, the missing-root code is aligned across commit and verify through one shared classifier, and the background path maps an absent leaf to the typed `capability_unavailable` with no probe, no spawn, and no directory write — while an existing-but-unsafe leaf keeps its custody code (`TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` rewritten, `TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid` added, narrowings `N-verify-absence-detail` / `N-background-absence-remap` / `N-root-missing-classify`).\\n- P2-C: the foreground Running arm is pinned at the entry for admission-empty servers — `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningWithEmptyAdmission` / `...WithEmptyGeneration` plus `N-running-empty-admission` / `N-running-empty-generation` (the reviewer's R01/R02 shapes, killing by a second spawn). P3-A: the TMUX collision member compares the socket component of the real `<socket>,<pid>,<index>` encoding at both levels (`N-collision-tmuxenv-encoding` drops the split). P3-C: root custody and \\\"AX-created\\\" stated as bounds B19/B20 with named owners (localstore layout creation, lifecycle bind step TASK-260830-1c28dz). P3-D: the `environ`-grammar comment corrected to what the code does and the always-nil `ObserveAmbient` error return dropped. P3-E: read-only-root (`runtime commit`, `N-commit-eacces-as-exist`, non-root bound) and whitespace-override rows added (`N-override-whitespace`, new rows 57/58). Observations: B15 gains the unreachable guard arm, B21 states the zero-UID broker model and generation-only socket binding, the `AfterMkdir` comment now says created-or-present.\\n- Battery: 54 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 56/56 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev4). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev3 — Private tmux server management rework (verify-side non-directory pin, both-empty arms, narrower-mode pin, cleaned collision)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2, five P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev1 finding stays closed). P2-A: the verify-side non-directory refusal is now pinned on the entry the background path uses — `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (0700 regular file admitted outright under the mutant; FIFO under a 5s deadline so the no-hang property pins too) plus `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` through the background entry, with harness row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` (kill signature: err-nil on both entries, 5s FIFO stall). Deliberate gate decision: the verify `Openat` carries no `O_NONBLOCK` — FIFO refusal relies on `O_DIRECTORY` failing fast, symmetric with the commit side, stated in TRACEABILITY row 5.\\n- P3-A: both-empty generation rows in both readiness tables plus `N-realm-empty-want` / `N-broker-empty-generation` (the broker row kills by reroute to the server-generation detail, disclosed in its note). P3-B: the narrower side of \\\"exactly 0700\\\" pinned — a pre-existing 0600/0500 leaf refuses `runtime mode` on both entries (`TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode`, `N-mode-narrower-create/verify`), so the exact-0700 prose stands as written. P3-C: the collision gate compares `filepath.Clean` spellings (one production-line change; `/./` and `//` aliases refused at `ResolveSocket` and through `Acquire`, `N-collision-unclean` drops `Clean`; symlink aliases bound B16). P3-D: the rev1 LOGBOOK block folded into rev2 (F1-F3 preserved, stale bullets replaced with a SUPERSEDED pointer). P3-E: stat-failure arms stated as bound B15 (error-arm rows, never counted as narrowings). Observations: import-census no-fallback bound under B9, Perm-only mode bound B17 (hosttrust precedent), `sun_path` bound B18 owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz.\\n- Battery: 46 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 48/48 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 55 of 55 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev3; row 5 names both entries, rows 4/23/36/38 name the new pins). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in 6 bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 64 pass / 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev2 — Private tmux server management rework (P1 attestation fork + Windows vet, 9 surviving narrowings)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev1 (CHANGES REQUESTED: 2 P1, 4 P2, 4 P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh). P1-A: `runtime_test.go` now carries `//go:build !windows` (it reassigns the unix-only `effectiveUID` seam and uses `syscall.Umask`); `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` is green (exit 0, run firsthand). P1-B: the forked `LiveAttestation`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`/`BrokerStatus` model is DELETED — `RealmAdmission` consumes the landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` verdict composed only with the `RawGeneration == Generation` equality `axpane.checkRealm` enforces, and the broker principal is a typed same-user UID plus generation-bound generation (no bare boolean); `Request.Hint`/`Cached`/`NeedsCredentials` are deleted with no replacement fields. The three reviewer holes now refuse through `Acquire`: wrong-generation foreground attach, wrong-generation broker contact, and a stale admission (the replayed-cached shape) on both paths.\\n- P2-A: nine surviving narrowings closed with committed killers + shipped rows — `Acquire` commit-phase refusal (`TestAcquireForegroundStagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-commit-refusal), background verify wiring (`TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-verify-refusal), verify-side symlink leaf (N-containment-symlink-verify), `TMUX_TMPDIR` override as the fifth vector (row 55, N-override-tmpdir), per-member collisions through `Acquire` (N-collision ×4), TMUX-env argv member (N-argv-tmuxenv), umask-0177 create proving the explicit `Fchmod` (N-fchmod-umask); the unreachable `ObserveAmbient` vocabulary arm is deleted. P2-B: `PlatformWindows` refuses at the lexical gate on every host (`tmux_invalid_arguments`); the Windows commit/verify arms are refusal stubs and the tripwire is deleted. P2-C: the decision-core-only split is a stated bound (B9, exec/probe adapters + socket crash evidence owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz) and the \\\"production wires\\\" sentence is deleted. P2-D: background acquisition verifies instead of ensuring (no durable write on the authorizing path); the dead foreground `checkCreationAllowed` call is deleted.\\n- P3: results now read the 30 commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` and report firsthand runs; crash convergence states the umask bound (B10); symlinked root intermediates state the secprim-matching bound (B11); the `CheckArgv` arm is covered by direct call with its Acquire-unreachability bound (B12). Battery: 40 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, twice with per-plant raw logs. AC: 55 of 55 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev2). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- FINDINGS carried forward from the rejected rev1 tree (the rev1 LOGBOOK block below is superseded and folded here; its DELIVERED/mutation/AC/bounds bullets described code deleted before trunk): F1 — a structural absence (\\\"this path has no spawn call\\\") is not an enforceable gate until a call exists to weaken, so the background miss path consults `checkCreationAllowed` by call (N-creation-literal reddens with the creation code, D-background-fallback reddens on the spy assertions). F2 — `Fchmod` before verification silently repairs, so the create path chmods only leaves it created while pre-existing leaves verify as-is (a widened `0755` refuses on both ensure and verify). F3 — single-member refusal classes narrow honestly (`caller == \\\"background\\\"` weakens to the capitalized twin; delegated scalar/secprim wirings narrow at our call site with reroute kills, never by re-testing the owner).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev1 (SUPERSEDED by the rev2 entry above — describes the rejected rev1 tree, never landed)\\n\\n- The rev1 block's DELIVERED/mutation/AC/bounds bullets are deleted: `CheckLiveAttestation`, four ambient vectors, the Windows creating-user ACL tripwire, 29 mutants, 54/54 rows, and 87.5% coverage describe the rejected rev1 design. Its findings F1-F3 are preserved in the rev2 entry above.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 49 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n- REV2 (rework of review RUN-260918-320878, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): P1-a CLOSED — envelope+body frame decodes delegate to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (lone-surrogate/duplicate/trailing faults refuse with the fault named; the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate); 4 new refusal rows + 4 narrowings. P2-c CLOSED — `bodyUint53` and the envelope version delegate to `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` (string-typed numbers refuse; per-member failures merge into one \\\"is not a uint53\\\" refusal while the ledger sum keeps \\\"exceeds uint53\\\"); string rows + 5 narrowings. New P3 rows: actor-order determinism (3 actors x12, `N-actors-sort`), both type/protection agreement arms, trailing bytes, protected-tool fold-skip, result-status vocabulary, size arm with its own message + drift row, unknown+protected body refusal; P3-i non-JSONL bound stated + pinned, P3-l null-directives pinned, P3-c per-edge rows stated as bounds (the \\\"representative\\\" claim removed); P3-j unions the 10.2 binding to 11 cases (10.2#2 gains `localstore-immutable-blob-install`); P3-k relabels (`N-empty-projection` single-member class, `N-overflow-truncate` behaviour swap). P2-a: one decision line per inherited advisory group (1,2,3,5,6,7b deferred with owners; 4/P3-e closed as a stated bound; 7a/P3-ζ closed by P1-a; 7c/P3-ζ′ rewritten as a deferred-unification bound) and the two false-prose sites rewritten. P2-b: 7.8#1 rebound to the new `session-adapter-frame-bound` case (`DecodeRequestFrame` + the oversize/edge tests, sessadapter owner); cases 144→145; digest re-derived `4bd01143…` gate-computed; README prose fixed (7.8 bound to sessadapter, Nine cases, admissions list, 10.2 union note).\\n- REV2 EVIDENCE: 62 narrowing + 2 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; the six re-anchorable reviewer plants (R1,R2,R5,R6,R7,R8 shapes) KILLED firsthand by the new tests. AC: 38 of 38 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev2).\\n- REV3 CORRECTION (rework of review RUN-260918-a4ffef, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): the REV2 sentence \\\"the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate\\\" was FALSE — the struct decode matched member names case-insensitively and took the last match, so a case-folded alias overrode the claimed value while the strict map admitted it as a distinct extra. The second decoder is DELETED: `parseNativeLine` now reads the six claimed envelope members from the strict map by exact name (`json.Unmarshal(members[name], ...)` + `Body = members[\\\"body\\\"]`), and no lenient re-read of the envelope remains anywhere after the strict gate (verified by grep: the only struct decode is gone; every other `Unmarshal` reads a strict-map member or a sealed manifest map by exact key).\\n- REV3 (same run): P1-b CLOSED — `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers` pins all six alias axes through `Normalize` (kind in both document orders, origin/authority, protection/promotion refusal, body/content, evidence identity, actor/attribution refusal) plus an unrelated-extra control; six `N-alias-*` narrowings each restore the case-folded read for exactly one member and all KILLED. P2-d CLOSED — positive `reasoning_summary` row (`TestNormalizeReasoningSummaryProjectsInternal`) + routing-swap narrowing. P3-m capture status asserted for every emitted kind (`TestNormalizeCaptureStatusExactForEveryKind` + partial-stamp narrowing); P3-n last-wins pinned by two native instructions (`TestNormalizeLastNativeInstructionWins` + fold-first narrowing); P3-o external kind pinned (`TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` + kind narrowing, and the reviewer-exact R7 swap KILLED firsthand); P3-p unknown-type-without-body refusal row + required-member narrowing (reviewer R1 shape); P3-q `text:null` stated as a bound (seals empty inline content, pinned) with `ciphertext:null` noted harmless; P3-r `N-pending-aborted` relabelled add-arm and the shared-site `N-strict-*` rows disclosed as one gate/two call sites (harness + TRACEABILITY + matrix + results); P3-s per-edge bound text now names `native_type` (reviewer R2 re-run firsthand: SURVIVED, inside the bound). Five prose sites corrected (`native.go` comments, TRACEABILITY rows, README exact-name sentence, this entry, results).\\n- REV3 EVIDENCE: 72 narrowing + 3 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; reviewer R1/R4/R5/R6 shapes adopted as shipped narrowings, R7 adopted as a condition narrowing with the exact swap also KILLED firsthand, R3 still KILLED (untouched line). AC: 45 of 45 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev3).\\n- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260918-d009f2, CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1; the rev2 rework is CLOSED AT THE CLASS per the verdict's Section 0 — kept untouched): P2-e CLOSED — `TestNormalizeMultiRecordRefsResolveAtAssertedOffsets` resolves EVERY event's `RawRefs[0]` against its own line with offsets asserted (`0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2`, multibyte first line), plus labelled behaviour-swap `N-offset-newline`; the reviewer's `RV-offset-line-number` and `RV-evidence-offset-second-line` shapes KILLED firsthand by the new row. P3-u/z pinned as bounds (`TestNormalizeNullOptionalBoolsDecodeAsFalse`, `TestNormalizeUnknownTypeNullBodyProjectsOpaque`); P3-v rows shipped (`body_text_number`, `body_live_attestation_string`, `body_missing_text` + 3 narrowings, the required gate pinned by its message); P3-w low edge pinned (`empty_directive` + `N-directive-empty`); P3-x `doc.go` nine→ten; P3-y declined-cosmetic with rationale (uniform member+line error shape is AC-pinned; the clonebundle helper wording at `session.go:527` is accepted sibling production, behavior verified correct); P3-aa MANIFEST self-entry dropped. No production change: test-plus-matrix only.\\n- REV4 REFRESH: trunk moved `c3aae73`→`42d5a95` (sibling STORY-260830-ptxkqe landed) before this run, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `42d5a95`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay for both checkpoints); the audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/fencing`, `internal/terminalbackend`) and MERGED the five co-owned files (LOGBOOK newest-first, README figures+prose, ownership registry 152 cases/74 rows with every trunk row intact, the four pin tests); `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` re-derived via the gate as `614eb55d…` (command+output in results); `tracecheck` green `70/574` with `--section 7.8`/`10.2` admitted. AC: 47 of 47 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev4).\\n- REV5 (rework of review RUN-260918-492d65, CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1; the ENTIRE rev3 rework is CLOSED and the refresh was a verified MERGE per the verdict's Section 0 — kept untouched; trunk unmoved at `42d5a95`, no refresh): P2-f CLOSED — the AC-named scale far edges are driven, not delegated: 65-parent / 1025-head / 1025-actor / 1000001-event-ID refusal rows at build AND decode in `internal/clonebundle` (each asserting code + message; otherwise-valid inputs so every build-side widening kills by admission), 8 widening narrowings (one per build/decode site, incl. the decode-actors row's missing narrowing), matrix section D and `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md` citing rows by name. P3-bb unterminated multi-line tail row (last event + offset asserted) + labelled drop row; P3-cc two per-type registry rows (`live_followup` on a call, `live_attestation` on a result) + narrowings with a seven-site census in results (the verdict says six; the tree carries seven maps); P3-dd output-axis usage overflow row + narrowing; P3-ee decode-side distinct-unsorted `raw_refs` row + narrowing; P3-ff CRLF stated beside the terminator sentence and pinned by a test; P3-gg matrix test-name fix + `forty-seven` dropped from the pin-test number map; P3-hh empty `subagent:` row + narrowing (honest message pin: the plant still refuses at the actor mapping). No production change: test-plus-matrix only.\\n- REV5 EVIDENCE: cloneproject battery 86/86 `ok:` twice (80 narrowings + 5 labelled KILLED + control SURVIVED), clonebundle battery 76/76 twice (75 + control), clonesnap 44/44 once (unchanged package), one raw log per plant per run with subprocess exits; `tracecheck` green `70/574` with `--section 7.8`/`10.2` admitted and the `614eb55d…` pin re-proven by the zeroed-pin gate print; full 30-command suite green (race gate in 7 bounded groups, 44/44 packages, no DATA RACE; full suite 2796 top-level PASS, +2 new tests). AC: 47 of 47 rows driven (matrix rev5; rows 4/10/23 extended, section D rewritten to cite rows).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm rev3 — Binding-parser rework: closed-shape arms, identity pre-transform walk, stated bounds\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (no P1; P2-1 production at the Binding parser, five P3; the reviewer reproduced the v4 payloads, evidence/identity/recovery/authority behavior, the registry re-pin, and the harness 30/30 twice — all kept). P2-1: `ParseTerminalBinding` now enforces `protocol_version` major 1 (`isProtocolMajorOne` over the landed semver grammar, verdict-agreed with `CheckVersionTuple` on a 14-version corpus) and `extensions == {}` (landed strict frame, zero members) per the §4.B table, and `bindingIdentity` refuses JSON numbers at any depth plus nested duplicate members before the JCS transform (strict UseNumber decode with per-depth dup refusal, mirroring the landed terminalbackend decode+walk — digest-equality and verdict agreement pinned, including a numeric extension value). Every member arm of the table is now driven negatively through the entry (37-subtest battery with code+detail pins) with six new narrowing rows (major, extensions, number, nested-dup, supersedes, pre-read generation bound). P3-2: `EmitResumed` checkpoint/pair binding stated explicitly as a caller bound with a boundary-pinning test (fabricated checkpoint appends; fold reports it newest). P3-3: generation-bound-before-read witness committed with its row. P3-4: pre-scan harness notes corrected to the documented redundancy, README bootstrap sentence corrected to the plain refusal, `resolve.go` \\\"every failure\\\" scoped to resolution failures, row 57 / 5.2#18 restated as a bound, descriptor test added to the identity-exact case. P3-5: restore/terminate-stale execution deferred to a Story follow-up task (no board task exists yet — no brief assigned it); the kkh1an `HandoffFailed` note is NOT APPLICABLE (this leaf wires no reporter).\\n- CORRECTION to the rev1 entry's F2 (appended, history preserved): \\\"the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals)\\\" is wrong for the two body surfaces — the landed `ParseMutationContext`/`ParseStatusBody` refuse a forbidden identity with the SAME pinned `terminal_backend_protocol_error`; the pre-scans add only the Go error type (`*terminalbackend.Error`), and no wrapper exists for the bootstrap surface at all (landed `Store.Bind` refuses plain and uncoded). The wrappers stay as a documented redundancy with corrected notes.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 28349,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 7088,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
