keeps its custody code. Kill path: the background ownership test asserts the top-level *Error the caller renders. [exit 1]\\nok: N-session-entry: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the PID-form session past the foreground-entry session arm; every other malformed session still refuses there, and the spawn-site arm still refuses the admitted member with the same code. Kill path: the admitted request creates the directory and probes the server before the spawn-site refusal, tripping the test's no-directory/no-probe assertions. [exit 1]\\nok: N-wiring-lexical: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the renamed leaf at the Acquire lexical site; the outcome socket becomes <root>/ax-tmux/ax.sock on both caller paths. Kill path: the entry-level spec-path test asserts the literal <root>/tmux/ax.sock. [exit 1]\\nok: N-wiring-ensure: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the renamed leaf at the foreground ensure site: the entry creates <root>/ax-tmux while the socket names <root>/tmux/ax.sock. Kill path: the socket-equality arm in BuildArgv refuses the mismatched pair, failing the foreground leg of the spec-path test. [exit 1]\\nok: N-wiring-verify: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the renamed leaf at the background verify site: the entry verifies <root>/ax-tmux (absent) while the socket names <root>/tmux/ax.sock. Kill path: the absent renamed leaf maps to the typed unavailable, failing the background leg of the spec-path test. [exit 1]\\nok: N-details-generation: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly generation-less requests past the typed-details arm; broker-less and remediation-less still refuse. Kill reroutes to the dependencies refusal. [exit 1]\\nok: N-details-brokerstate: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly broker-state-less requests past the typed-details arm; generation-less and remediation-less still refuse. Kill reroutes to the dependencies refusal. [exit 1]\\nok: N-details-constructor: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the invalid-UTF-8 generation past the refusal-renderer arm: the constructor failure is swallowed and the miss reports success with a zero outcome. Kill path: the detail test expects the invalid-arguments refusal and gets nil. [exit 1]\\nok: D-background-fallback-foreground: KILLED (want KILLED) :: SUPPLEMENTARY ADDITIVE, not a narrowing: a fallback into acquireForeground on the background miss path, guarded on the foreground probe dependency — the shared-Dependencies shape, where the lifecycle adapter passes one Dependencies value to every caller. Kill path: every background-miss test arms both a spy spawner and a spy server probe and asserts the typed unavailable, so re-entering the foreground path trips the census before it spawns. [exit 1]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3408,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 852,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
