orm past our wiring of the landed vocabulary; every other unknown platform still refuses. One shared site, both custody entries: kill reroutes to the root refusal on each. [exit 1]\\nok: N-platform-windows: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the C: fixture root past the lexical Windows refusal; every other Windows root still refuses there. Kill reroutes to the root refusal, which reports runtime root instead of runtime platform. [exit 1]\\nok: N-argv-session: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the PID-form session past our wiring of the landed UUIDv7 grammar at the spawn site; every other malformed session still refuses. The Acquire-level killer passes under this plant — the foreground entry refuses before the spawn site — so the kill comes from the direct BuildArgv test; the entry arm carries its own row N-session-entry. [exit 1]\\nok: D-background-fallback: KILLED (want KILLED) :: SUPPLEMENTARY ADDITIVE, not a narrowing: plants the reviewer-shaped direct-creation call on the background miss path. Kill path: every background-miss spy asserts zero spawn calls. [exit 1]\\nok: C-control: SURVIVED (want SURVIVED) :: Harmless control: a comment-only edit that must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes outcomes. [exit 0]\\n===\\n M LOGBOOK.md\\n M README.md\\n A internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md\\n A internal/tmuxserver/acquire.go\\n A internal/tmuxserver/acquire_test.go\\n A internal/tmuxserver/argv.go\\n A internal/tmuxserver/argv_test.go\\n A internal/tmuxserver/crash_unix_test.go\\n A internal/tmuxserver/doc.go\\n A internal/tmuxserver/errors.go\\nhygiene-done\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2155,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 539,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
