{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d557","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c54c-0ef4-78b3-96e2-4f10155428e6"},"sequence":2310,"recorded_at":1780531400004615,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c569-e912-7860-aec4-58b48fe58c00"},"task_id":"01a0c569-e912-7860-aec4-58b48fe58c00","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c569-e912-7860-aec4-58b48fe58c00","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-21\n-\n-### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\n+## 2026-09-21\n+\n+### TASK-260830-35urbp rev6 — Gate × entry census instrument + broker-wiring, ownership, and session-entry pins\n+\n+- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev5 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2 class with four measured members, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev4 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove). The deliverable this round is the instrument: a gate × entry census (24 gates × 11 entries = 264 cells: 50 measured with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row each, 4 stated bounds, 210 unreachable with structural reasons) in TRACEABILITY.md, mirrored in the conformance matrix. Building it surfaced and closed member gaps beyond the four the reviewer measured.\n+- P2-A (broker-or-refuse pinned at the entry only for fixture shapes): three server-admission subtests (zero admission, admitted-without-generation, decoy-only) added to `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` AND mirrored in `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`; shipped `N-broker-zero-admission` at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (R09 shape; R10/R19 share the anchor — replay-verified killed by the new tests); a fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy armed in every background-path `Acquire` test (22/22 mechanical census, incl. the miss tables and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`); shipped `D-background-fallback-foreground` (R18 shape: fallback into `acquireForeground` guarded on `ProbeServer`) with the row-31/README sentence extended to both foreground dependencies.\n+- P3-A (ownership member of the absence class): new `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (unix-only file, `effectiveUID` seam) asserting the top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership` with no broker contact and both spies silent, plus shipped `N-absence-remap-ownership` (R01 shape); the census added the sibling rows `N-absence-remap-containment` and `N-absence-remap-invalid` so every classifier member carries a row. P3-B (false \"before any side effect\"): session identity now parses at the foreground entry before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe, with no-directory/no-probe assertions in `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` and shipped `N-session-entry` (kills through the side-effect assertions while the refusal code stays correct).\n+- Census-driven closures beyond the verdict: caller-dimension subtests on the pre-dispatch gates (override/collision/details/unknown-platform tables drive both callers); `N-dispatch-foreground`/`N-dispatch-background` for the caller→path routing; `N-wiring-lexical/ensure/verify` for the three `RuntimeDirName` sites; `N-details-generation/brokerstate/constructor` (incl. the input-reachable invalid-UTF-8 arm, pinned with a probe-order assertion); `N-root-symlink-commit/verify` plus verify- and background-entry symlink-root tests; `N-argv-detached/tail` with a full element-by-element vector assertion through the spawn entry; background-entry symlink-leaf and handle-mismatch tests; mask extensions so shared-site rows kill through every entry they cover (attribution verified per entry from the raw logs).\n+- Observations: row 23/B16 scope comma roots out of the TMUX member's encoding and symlinked-or-relative aliases out of the cleaned-string gate; B9 states `Dependencies.Spawn` as inert on the background path; B15 names the commit-side leaf-`Stat` and `NewGuard` arms; static-gate exit codes recorded in the evidence archive.\n+- Battery: 72 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 75/75 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev6). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in one call per the configured command, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\n","final_result":true}}}
