{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e05d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c54c-0ef4-78b3-96e2-4f10155428e6"},"sequence":3721,"recorded_at":1780531400007437,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a845ab6a-f3a6-48e7-a9d4-e4e3621097f9"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — revision 6 of TASK-260830-35urbp handed off (`to-review`, checklist 19/19, candidate uncommitted in the Story worktree).\n\nWhat was delivered:\n\n- **Gate × entry census (the brief's instrument):** 24 gates × 11 entries = 264 cells — 50 measured with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row each, 4 stated bounds, 210 unreachable with structural reasons. Full table in the conformance matrix, mirrored byte-identically in `TRACEABILITY.md`. Counts, test/row references, and the mirror verified by script.\n- **P2-A:** three server-admission shapes (zero, admitted-without-generation, decoy-only) pinned in the background miss table and mirrored in the broker-contact table; shipped `N-broker-zero-admission` (R10/R19 share the anchor — replay-verified killed); `ProbeServer` spy armed in all 23 background-path tests; shipped `D-background-fallback-foreground`; row-31/README sentence extended to both dependencies.\n- **P3-A:** `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` + `N-absence-remap-ownership`, plus sibling containment/invalid classifier rows.\n- **P3-B:** session parses at the foreground entry before any side effect, with no-directory/no-probe assertions + `N-session-entry`.\n- **Census-driven extras:** caller-dimension subtests on pre-dispatch gates, dispatch narrowings both directions, per-site wiring narrowings, constructor/detail rows, root-symlink rows + tests, full argv vector assertion through the entry, background symlink-leaf/mismatch/root tests, and run-mask extensions with per-entry kill attribution verified from raw logs.\n\nEvidence: 58/58 AC rows driven; battery 75/75 twice with identical verdicts (72 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED, control SURVIVED); package suite 190/190, 0 skip, including tmux-hidden with env proof; all 30 validation commands green firsthand (race in 6 bounded groups with identical flags, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows` vet/test-compile green; evidence tarball (193 MANIFEST entries, all verified, no self-entry) attached with byte-identical sha256.","reason":null}}
